phagia screening methods and clinical assessments, and she explores the intersection of internet technology and health, particularly in relation to dysphagia.CARMEN G√ìMEZ TRIGUERO:Carmen G√≥mez Triguero is a Specialist Physician in the Rehabilitation Service at the Hospital Universitario Pr√≠ncipe de Asturias. She is actively involved in research concerning oropharyngeal dysphagia rehabilitation, contributing as a co-author to various studies in this field. Additionally, she has played a significant role in developing a manual that addresses solutions for oropharyngeal dysphagia, with a particular focus on exercises designed for orofacial structures that are crucial for the swallowing process. Through her work, Carmen G√≥mez Triguero has established herself as a key contributor to the understanding and treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia.MONTSERRAT MART√çNEZ LI√âBANA:Montserrat Mart√≠nez Li√©bana is a Senior Technician in Dietetics and Nutrition at the Hospital Universitario Pr√≠ncipe de Asturias.LOURDES MONEVA VICENTE:Lourdes Moneva Vicente is a dedicated nurse in the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at the Hospital Universitario Pr√≠ncipe de Asturias. She specializes in the nutritional treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia, providing essential nursing care for patients affected by this condition. In addition to her clinical work, Lourdes is also a co-author of a document that emphasizes the importance of oral hygiene, highlighting her commitment to improving patient care and outcomes in her field.NATASHA P√âREZ MARRERO:Natasha P√©rez Marrero is a Specialist Physician in the Otolaryngology Service at the Hospital Universitario Pr√≠ncipe de Asturias. She is recognized for her contributions to the clinical guidelines on dysphagia, indicating her expertise in the field of otolaryngology.TERESA RIVERA RODR√çGUEZ:Teresa Rivera Rodr√≠guez is a prominent figure in the field of otolaryngology, serving as the Head of the Otolaryngology Service at the Hospital Universitario Pr√≠ncipe de Asturias. In addition to her leadership role, she is also an Associate Professor of Health Sciences. Her expertise is further demonstrated through her contributions to clinical guidelines on dysphagia, indicating her significant involvement and knowledge in this specialized area of medicine.MANUAL DE DISFAGIA OROFAR√çNGEA:The "Manual de Disfagia Orofaringea" is a comprehensive guide designed to address oropharyngeal dysphagia through a multidisciplinary approach. It offers a wide range of solutions for the assessment, diagnosis, and treatment of this swallowing disorder, focusing on various aspects such as hydration, nutritional therapy, dietary adaptations, and rehabilitation strategies.

The manual includes detailed information on diagnostic scales and evaluation techniques for swallowing disorders, as well as clinical history considerations, gastrointestinal symptoms, and functional capacity assessments. It emphasizes the importance of tailored dietary recommendations, including texture modifications and liquid viscosities, to meet the nutritional needs of individuals with oropharyngeal dysphagia.

In addition to dietary guidelines, the manual provides practical solutions such as recipes and cooking techniques specifically designed for patients with swallowing difficulties. It also discusses exercises and techniques aimed at improving muscle strength and swallowing function, particularly for those affected by neurological conditions, head and neck cancer, or post-stroke recovery.

Furthermore, the "Manual de Disfagia Orofaringea" addresses safety protocols in food preparation, allergen management, and oral hygiene practices, ensuring comprehensive care for patients. It serves as a valuable resource for healthcare professionals and caregivers involved in the management of oropharyngeal dysphagia, particularly in elderly patients and those with complex medical needs.VIRGINIA RODR√çGUEZ CAMPUZANO:Virginia Rodr√≠guez Campuzano is a dedicated nurse in the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at the Hospital Universitario Pr√≠ncipe de Asturias, where she specializes in the care of patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia. In her role, she is actively involved in providing nursing care tailored to the needs of these patients. Additionally, Virginia has contributed to the field through her research on multidisciplinary solutions for oropharyngeal dysphagia, highlighting her commitment to advancing knowledge and practices in this area. She is also a co-author of a document emphasizing the importance of oral hygiene, further showcasing her dedication to improving patient care and health outcomes.MANUEL RODR√çGUEZ PARADINAS:Manuel Rodr√≠guez Paradinas is a prominent figure in the field of oropharyngeal dysphagia rehabilitation, serving as a co-author and contributor to clinical guidelines related to dysphagia. He is recognized as an expert in otolaryngology and plays a vital role in the multidisciplinary team at the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar√≠ngea. His research interests include studying the impact of digital technology on health and dysphagia, highlighting his commitment to advancing knowledge in this area. Additionally, he specializes in the Otolaryngology Service and is responsible for overseeing the Oropharyngeal Dysphagia Functional Unit at the Hospital Universitario Pr√≠ncipe de Asturias. Through his work, Manuel Rodr√≠guez Paradinas focuses on the treatment and evaluation of oropharyngeal dysphagia, contributing significantly to the understanding and management of this condition.PAULA ROMERO CORT√âS:Paula Romero Cort√©s is a medical resident specializing in Endocrinology and Nutrition at the Hospital Universitario Pr√≠ncipe de Asturias. In addition to her clinical training, she is also an author who contributes to the understanding of nutritional support for patients with dysphagia, highlighting her commitment to improving patient care through both practice and research.MAR√çA DOLORES VALVERDE CARRILLO:Mar√≠a Dolores Valverde Carrillo is a prominent figure in the field of oropharyngeal dysphagia, contributing significantly to both research and clinical practice. She is a member of the team at the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar√≠ngea, where she focuses on patient care and rehabilitation. As the head of the Rehabilitation Service and an associate professor of Health Sciences at the University of Alcal√° (UAH), she plays a crucial role in the study and treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia.

