=ãê¬ºhÜíºlÇº´Ôºi»íº™dÓ<åDºj¨=lòΩ¨®Ò;aúΩfXè<l2º¨‘q<ñ“ºû<ﬁ:p¿=z0´<§Ãeª]$É;zÿ™ºhZíºh™ëºkNñ<Æ¿Ùº`÷º~4±<z¬*<s‡†ºg4<`áºyb©ºkêñºyé)∫Ñ¯πºáî=<y§)<èîHºd*å<`~<xD(ªeHçºØpu<x÷ßº`hÜ<|ò≠;™ênºá¿=Ω°¨aºê»I=ìòŒ<_ŒÖ=®Lk<µå~;u®$=â§?=^íΩdVΩôÿ÷;^ÑΩ[NÄºc 
<u‚£<}$Ø<±¥x<õlŸªrû†<Ç7=àD>º±àx;w`¶;ù,‹:ä8Bºüp_ºÄÙ3<fnè7lló;^|É;u$ºØLˆ;<≤<¶hÈ;ìlN∏åC<ödÿºu†£∫e2;ef<î$–ºn∆ö:|⁄≠<x.®8pºöêÿª`¿Ü=©àÌºhZíºô0Wºâ–øºé`G<°‚∫≠‹Ú<¨Pqº`÷Üº´HpΩtÆ¢ºáhΩ<wh'ªµ∞}ºu|§:a =|Ç-=~X∞<µå˛:{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO PR\u00cdNCIPE DE ASTURIAS:The Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias (HUPA) is a prominent medical facility located in Alcal\u00e1 de Henares, Madrid. It specializes in various medical fields, particularly endocrinology and nutrition, with Julia \u00c1lvarez Hern\u00e1ndez serving as the Head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Section. In addition to its focus on endocrinology, HUPA is recognized for its comprehensive management of oropharyngeal dysphagia, having established the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar\u00edngea (UFDOF) to address the needs of patients suffering from this condition.\n\nThe hospital employs a multidisciplinary approach to provide acute care and optimize the quality of care for patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia. This includes the development of 36 specialized recipes aimed at managing the dietary needs of these patients. HUPA is committed to integrating various medical services to ensure comprehensive patient care, making it a pioneering institution in the treatment of dysphagia. Overall, the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias plays a vital role in both endocrinology and the management of dysphagia, contributing significantly to the healthcare landscape in Madrid."}{"title": "SENPE:SENPE, or Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Nutrici\u00f3n Cl\u00ednica y Metabolismo, is a prominent Spanish society dedicated to the fields of clinical nutrition and metabolism. This professional organization plays a crucial role in addressing hospital malnutrition in Spain, providing essential documentation and management strategies. SENPE collaborates with SEMICYUC to develop updated recommendations for critical care nutrition, ensuring that healthcare professionals have access to the latest guidelines for nutritional support.\n\nIn addition to its focus on clinical nutrition, SENPE is actively involved in standardizing practices related to pediatric enteral nutrition. The organization works on creating consensus documents that outline best practices and guidelines for pediatric nutrition, thereby enhancing the quality of care for young patients. SENPE also engages in discussions and provides guidelines related to enteral nutrition and diet therapy, further solidifying its role as a key player in the nutritional landscape of Spain.\n\nMoreover, SENPE is recognized as the Spanish Society of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition, emphasizing its commitment to nutritional care in hospital settings. This includes the development of guidelines and consensus documents that inform nutritional practices for both parenteral and enteral nutrition. The society also supports scientific initiatives, such as the publication on oropharyngeal dysphagia, highlighting its dedication to advancing knowledge and practices in the field of nutrition.\n\nOverall, SENPE serves as a vital resource for healthcare professionals in Spain, promoting best practices in clinical nutrition, pediatric nutrition, and nutritional support in various healthcare settings."}{"title": "AEHH:AEHH, or Asociaci\u00f3n Espa\u00f1ola de Hosteler\u00eda, is a Spanish association focused on the hospitality sector. It is also known as the Asociaci\u00f3n Espa\u00f1ola de Hosteler\u00eda Hospitalaria, which is a scientific society that supports research and knowledge dissemination related to oropharyngeal dysphagia. This dual identity highlights AEHH's commitment to both the hospitality industry and the medical field, particularly in addressing issues related to swallowing disorders."}{"title": "SEEN:SEEN, or Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n, is a prominent Spanish society dedicated to the fields of endocrinology and nutrition. This organization plays a crucial role in the study and treatment of endocrine and nutritional disorders, contributing significantly to the development of clinical guidelines and evidence-based practices. SEEN is involved in various aspects of clinical nutrition, including the publication of texts and resources that support professionals in the field. \n\nThe society is particularly focused on issues related to obesity and diabetes, engaging in clinical trials and research that enhance understanding and treatment of these conditions. SEEN also provides educational resources, including materials related to dysphagia, and endorses scientific literature, such as the book on oropharyngeal dysphagia. With a commitment to advancing knowledge and practice in endocrinology and nutrition, SEEN supports education and research initiatives, making it a vital organization in the health landscape of Spain."}{"title": "ADENYD:ADENYD, or the Asociaci\u00f3n de Enfermeras de Nutrici\u00f3n y Diet\u00e9tica, is a scientific society based in Spain that focuses on the fields of nutrition and dietetics. The organization is dedicated to supporting various initiatives, including the production of a book on oropharyngeal dysphagia. It serves as a professional association for nurses who specialize in nutrition and dietetics, promoting best practices and advancements in these areas."}{"title": "GU\u00cdAM\u00c9DICA FORMACI\u00d3N EN SALUD:gu\u00edam\u00e9dica formaci\u00f3n en salud is an organization that provides health training and resources."}{"title": "VEGENAT HEALTHCARE:Vegenat HEALTHCARE is an organization involved in healthcare solutions, as indicated by its logo in the document."}{"title": "DISFAGIA OROFAR\u00cdNGEA:Disfagia orofar\u00edngea (DOF), or oropharyngeal dysphagia, is a medical condition characterized by difficulty in swallowing, which can significantly impact a patient's nutrition and quality of life. This condition often necessitates dietary adaptations in texture and viscosity to ensure safe swallowing, as well as specific care strategies during feeding to prevent complications such as aspiration pneumonia, malnutrition, and dehydration. \n\nDisfagia orofar\u00edngea is commonly observed in patients with various medical conditions, including stroke, and it requires a multidisciplinary approach for effective assessment, rehabilitation, and management. Healthcare professionals utilize various diagnostic tests, such as pH-impedance and manometry, to evaluate the severity of the condition. Early detection and treatment are crucial, as untreated DOF can lead to serious health consequences.\n\nThe management of oropharyngeal dysphagia involves not only dietary modifications but also rehabilitation techniques and specific nursing care to ensure safe oral feeding. It is relevant in hospital settings, particularly in food service and preparation, where understanding the dietary needs of affected patients is essential. Additionally, the condition is the focus of various health data collection and management systems, highlighting its significance in clinical practice and research.\n\nOverall, oropharyngeal dysphagia is a complex swallowing disorder that requires comprehensive care strategies to enhance patient outcomes and maintain nutritional health."}{"title": "GRUPO AULA M\u00c9DICA, S.L.:Grupo Aula M\u00e9dica, S.L. is the publishing house responsible for the edition of the book on oropharyngeal dysphagia."}{"title": "JULIA \u00c1LVAREZ HERN\u00c1NDEZ:Julia \u00c1lvarez Hern\u00e1ndez is a prominent medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition, serving as the Head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Section at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias in Alcal\u00e1 de Henares, Madrid. In her role, she is actively involved in the management and treatment of patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia, working within the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar\u00edngea. Julia is also a co-author and coordinator of a book discussing oropharyngeal dysphagia, contributing her expertise to the section that addresses this condition. Her work encompasses a broad range of topics related to nutrition and dysphagia, highlighting her commitment to advancing knowledge and treatment in these fields."}{"title": "ESPA\u00d1A:Espa\u00f1a es un pa\u00eds europeo que ha sido el escenario de importantes investigaciones y programas relacionados con la salud y la nutrici\u00f3n. Uno de los estudios m\u00e1s destacados es el Proyecto PREDIMED, un ensayo cl\u00ednico que investiga la dieta mediterr\u00e1nea y su impacto en la salud cardiovascular. Sin embargo, Espa\u00f1a enfrenta desaf\u00edos significativos en t\u00e9rminos de salud p\u00fablica, como el aumento de la obesidad, que ha duplicado su tasa en los \u00faltimos 20 a\u00f1os, superando actualmente el 20% de la poblaci\u00f3n.\n\nEn el \u00e1mbito de la nutrici\u00f3n, se ha observado una prevalencia de nutrici\u00f3n parenteral en adultos de 5,06 pacientes por mill\u00f3n de habitantes. Adem\u00e1s, se han realizado estudios sobre la prevalencia de enfermedades respiratorias como la EPOC y las bronquiectasias, reportando cifras significativas de casos por cada 10,000 habitantes. En cuanto a la cirug\u00eda bari\u00e1trica, Espa\u00f1a lleva a cabo t\u00e9cnicas como el bypass g\u00e1strico y la gastrectom\u00eda vertical laparosc\u00f3pica para tratar la obesidad.\n\nEl pa\u00eds tambi\u00e9n regula la autonom\u00eda del paciente y sus derechos en relaci\u00f3n con la informaci\u00f3n y documentaci\u00f3n cl\u00ednica, incluyendo decisiones sobre nutrici\u00f3n artificial. A nivel demogr\u00e1fico, Espa\u00f1a tiene un 18.2% de su poblaci\u00f3n mayor de 65 a\u00f1os, cifra que se proyecta aumentar\u00e1 al 24.9% para 2029 y al 38.7% para 2064.\n\nEn el \u00e1mbito de la salud digital, Espa\u00f1a se est\u00e1 convirtiendo en un actor clave, especialmente en el tratamiento de la disfagia. Sin embargo, el pa\u00eds enfrenta dificultades para cumplir con las recomendaciones internacionales sobre la ingesta de grasas saturadas, que actualmente superan el 10%. Aproximadamente el 10% de la poblaci\u00f3n adulta padece alg\u00fan grado de enfermedad renal cr\u00f3nica, y la litiasis biliar es la causa m\u00e1s com\u00fan de pancreatitis aguda, especialmente entre mujeres de mediana edad.\n\nEn cuanto a la diabetes, cerca de 30,000 menores de 15 a\u00f1os sufren de Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1, y se han reportado tasas significativas de trastornos alimentarios. Los estudios tambi\u00e9n indican que la poblaci\u00f3n consume niveles de omega-3 cercanos a los recomendados, aunque presenta una alta relaci\u00f3n omega-6 a omega-3. La dieta mediterr\u00e1nea ha demostrado beneficios significativos para la salud, especialmente en la salud cardiovascular.\n\nLa ingesta promedio de potasio en Espa\u00f1a es de"}{"title": "DISFAGIA:Dysphagia is a medical condition characterized by difficulty in swallowing, affecting individuals across various age groups and often associated with a range of underlying health issues, including neurological disorders, head and neck tumors, and esophageal conditions. This condition can manifest as challenges in swallowing both solid and liquid foods, leading to significant nutritional risks, complications such as aspiration, and potential malnutrition. \n\nDysphagia is prevalent in approximately 3% of the general population and is particularly common among patients with specific medical conditions, such as stroke, multiple sclerosis, and esophageal cancer. It can severely impact a patient's quality of life and dietary choices, necessitating specialized dietary modifications and interventions by healthcare professionals. \n\nManagement of dysphagia often requires a multidisciplinary approach, including nutritional assessment, the use of thickeners, and enteral nutrition in more severe cases. The condition is also gaining attention in the context of digital health solutions, highlighting the need for effective assessment and treatment strategies. \n\nOverall, dysphagia is a complex condition that requires careful evaluation and tailored interventions to ensure safe swallowing and adequate nutritional intake, making it a critical focus in both clinical practice and research."}{"title": "AULAMEDICA FORMACION EN SALUD:"}{"title": "UNIDAD FUNCIONAL DE DISFAGIA OROFAR\u00cdNGEA:The Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar\u00edngea (UFDOF) is a specialized, multidisciplinary unit established in 2013 within the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias (HUPA). Its primary focus is on the assessment, diagnosis, and treatment of patients suffering from oropharyngeal dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. The unit aims to provide comprehensive care through collaborative efforts among various healthcare professionals, ensuring that patients receive tailored and effective management for their swallowing disorders. UFDOF emphasizes quality care and integrates multiple disciplines to enhance the treatment and rehabilitation processes for individuals with dysphagia, thereby improving their adapted nutrition and overall well-being."}{"title": "VEGENAT\u00ae HEALTHCARE:Vegenat\u00ae Healthcare is a company that provided unconditional support for the creation of the book on oropharyngeal dysphagia."}{"title": "JAVIER COELLO:Javier Coello is the editor who worked on the book, contributing to its production and ensuring its timely release."}{"title": "DISFAGIA OROFAR\u00cdNGEA: SOLUCIONES MULTIDISCIPLINARES:The book titled *Disfagia orofar\u00edngea: soluciones multidisciplinares* addresses the treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia and aims to be a reference in the field."}{"title": "PACIENTES:PACIENTES refers to a diverse group of individuals facing various medical conditions that necessitate specialized nutritional support and dietary management. This group includes individuals suffering from chronic respiratory diseases such as EPOC (Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease), cystic fibrosis (FQ), and bronchiectasis (BQ), who often encounter nutritional challenges. Additionally, patients with celiac disease must adhere to a strict gluten-free diet and receive education about their condition and associated risks.\n\nCertain patients are at risk of refeeding syndrome, particularly those with a history of malnutrition, anorexia nervosa, or prolonged fasting, requiring careful monitoring and nutritional support. Others may need artificial nutrition at home due to an inability to meet their nutritional needs through regular food intake. This includes patients undergoing surgical procedures related to the digestive system, such as gastrostomy or jejunostomy, who require tailored nutritional support post-surgery.\n\nPACIENTES also encompasses individuals with food allergies or intolerances, who need appropriate information and treatment. Those suffering from conditions like dysphagia, particularly oropharyngeal dysphagia, face challenges in swallowing and require specialized care and management. This group includes patients receiving treatment in specialized units, such as the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar\u00edngea, where their treatment and satisfaction are prioritized.\n\nFurthermore, patients with gastrointestinal disorders, such as Crohn's disease or ulcerative colitis, may require nutritional support to manage their conditions effectively. Individuals suffering from acute pancreatitis also undergo various treatments and nutritional assessments. \n\nIn the context of eating disorders, PACIENTES includes individuals with anorexia nervosa and bulimia nervosa, who face both psychological and nutritional challenges and require comprehensive dietary education and support. Additionally, patients with urea cycle disorders, who experience symptoms like hyperammonemia, necessitate dietary management and treatment.\n\nOverall, PACIENTES represents a broad spectrum of individuals requiring medical treatment and specialized nutritional care due to various health conditions, emphasizing the importance of individualized dietary plans and support systems tailored to their unique needs."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N:NUTRICI\u00d3N refers to the comprehensive field of study and practice focused on the dietary needs and health of individuals, particularly in clinical settings. It encompasses the processes involved in the intake, assimilation, and utilization of nutrients, which are crucial for health, growth, and recovery. Nutritional support is essential for various patient populations, including those undergoing treatments for cancer, managing chronic diseases, or recovering from surgeries. \n\nIn the context of specific health conditions, NUTRICI\u00d3N plays a vital role in managing the dietary needs of patients with cancer, particularly during chemotherapy and radiotherapy, where adequate nutrition can help prevent complications such as cachexia and improve quality of life. It is also critical for patients with digestive disorders, such as pancreatitis, and those with conditions like dysphagia, where dietary modifications are necessary to ensure safe and effective feeding.\n\nThe importance of nutrition extends to vulnerable populations, including the elderly, where tailored dietary interventions can prevent malnutrition and frailty. Nutritional assessments and interventions are crucial for improving health outcomes, particularly in patients with acute renal failure, eating disorders, and those experiencing significant weight loss due to various medical conditions.\n\nNUTRICI\u00d3N also emphasizes the significance of providing adequate nutrition for infants, especially preterm and newborns, to support their growth and development. The field includes research and evidence-based practices aimed at understanding the relationship between dietary habits and health, as well as the ethical considerations involved in nutritional support and patient participation in care decisions.\n\nOverall, NUTRICI\u00d3N is a critical aspect of healthcare that integrates dietary management, nutritional education, and clinical practices to enhance patient recovery and well-being across diverse health contexts."}{"title": "REHABILITACI\u00d3N:Rehabilitaci\u00f3n refers to the comprehensive process of rehabilitation that is often associated with enteral nutrition, aimed at helping patients regain their ability to eat orally. This process is particularly important for individuals suffering from oropharyngeal dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. Rehabilitation for oropharyngeal dysphagia involves the implementation of specific techniques and strategies designed to enhance swallowing safety and efficiency. The Rehabilitaci\u00f3n (Rehabilitation) service is dedicated to the recovery and treatment of patients with various conditions, including those experiencing dysphagia. The Rehabilitation department provides targeted therapeutic interventions to improve the swallowing function of these patients, ensuring a holistic approach to their care and recovery."}{"title": "OTORRINOLARINGOLOG\u00cdA:Otorrrinolaringolog\u00eda, also known as otolaryngology, is a medical specialty dedicated to the evaluation and treatment of disorders related to the ear, nose, and throat. This specialty encompasses a range of conditions, including those affecting swallowing and the glosopalatine function of patients. The department plays a crucial role in diagnosing and managing dysphagia-related conditions, particularly oropharyngeal dysphagia, ensuring comprehensive care for individuals experiencing difficulties in these areas."}{"title": "CUIDADORES:CUIDADORES, or caregivers, are individuals who play a crucial role in providing care to patients, particularly those with health conditions such as disfagia orofar\u00edngea (oropharyngeal dysphagia) and chronic illnesses. Often family members, caregivers support patients receiving nutritional therapy at home and help manage their daily care needs. They also address the psychological and emotional challenges faced by these patients, especially the elderly who may be frail. The involvement of caregivers significantly impacts the overall well-being of the individuals they assist, highlighting their importance in the healthcare system."}{"title": "F\u00c9LIX BRAVO SANZ:F\u00e9lix Bravo Sanz is the Director Manager of the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias. In this role, he oversees the hospital's operations and initiatives, including specific efforts related to oropharyngeal dysphagia. His leadership is integral to the management and strategic direction of the hospital, ensuring that various health initiatives are effectively implemented."}{"title": "ENFERMEDADES NEUROL\u00d3GICAS:\"ENFERMEDADES NEUROL\u00d3GICAS\" refers to a range of disorders that significantly impact the nervous system and are a major health concern in developed countries. These diseases can lead to various complications, including altered consciousness and difficulties with swallowing, known as dysphagia. As a result, many patients suffering from neurological diseases may require artificial nutritional support, specifically enteral nutrition, to meet their dietary needs. Conditions such as Parkinson's disease, amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, and Alzheimer's disease are notable examples of neurological disorders that can severely impair the ability to eat normally, necessitating this form of nutritional intervention. Overall, neurological diseases present complex challenges that often require specialized care and support for affected individuals."}{"title": "QUIMIOTERAPIA:QUIMIOTERAPIA, or chemotherapy, is an aggressive treatment method for cancer that employs powerful drugs to kill cancer cells. It is commonly used in various contexts, including before hematopoietic stem cell transplantation and in the management of specific cancers such as pancreatic cancer. While effective in targeting cancer, chemotherapy often leads to significant side effects that can adversely affect a patient's nutritional status and overall quality of life. \n\nPatients undergoing chemotherapy may experience complications such as oropharyngeal dysphagia, hyperglycemia, cachexia, nausea, vomiting, and mucositis, which can hinder normal food intake and may necessitate enteral nutrition. The treatment can also result in nutritional deficiencies and weight changes, including loss of appetite. As a result, careful management of the patient's nutritional needs is crucial during chemotherapy to mitigate these adverse effects and support recovery. \n\nIn summary, QUIMIOTERAPIA is a vital but challenging component of cancer treatment, requiring close attention to the patient's health and nutritional status throughout the process."}{"title": "RADIOTERAPIA:RADIOTERAPIA, or radiotherapy, is a treatment method that employs high doses of radiation to eliminate cancer cells. It is frequently utilized in the management of neoplasms and may be considered as a treatment option following surgery. While effective in targeting cancer, radiotherapy can have significant adverse effects on a patient's nutritional status. These effects can manifest as acute and chronic nutritional complications, which are influenced by factors such as the tumor's location and the radiation dose administered.\n\nPatients undergoing radiotherapy may experience side effects like mucositis, which can hinder their ability to consume adequate nutrition. Additionally, the treatment can lead to oropharyngeal dysphagia, particularly in individuals with head and neck cancers, further complicating their nutritional intake. There is also a risk of damage to the pituitary gland, potentially resulting in hormonal deficiencies such as hypopituitarism.\n\nOverall, while RADIOTERAPIA is a critical component of cancer treatment, it is essential to monitor and manage the nutritional implications that arise during the course of therapy to ensure the well-being of patients."}{"title": "NEUMON\u00cdAS POR ASPIRACI\u00d3N:Aspiration pneumonia is a serious complication that can arise from oropharyngeal dysphagia, leading to high mortality rates."}{"title": "DESHIDRATACI\u00d3N:\"DESHIDRATACI\u00d3N\" refers to dehydration, a condition that occurs when the body loses more fluids than it takes in, which can significantly affect overall health and performance. It is a common consequence of various medical conditions, including watery diarrhea, particularly in patients with a congenital deficit of saccharase-isomaltase. Dehydration can also arise from oropharyngeal dysphagia, which complicates the clinical situation for affected patients, as well as from difficulties in swallowing and eating, especially in individuals with head and neck tumors. Additionally, patients undergoing enteral nutrition may experience dehydration due to negative fluid balance, leading to symptoms such as dryness of the skin and mucous membranes. Proper hydration is crucial, particularly during exercise, to prevent dehydration and its associated health risks. Overall, dehydration is a serious condition that can lead to significant health issues if not properly managed."}{"title": "DESNUTRICI\u00d3N:\"DESNUTRICI\u00d3N\" refers to a medical condition characterized by a deficiency of essential nutrients, which can significantly impact health and recovery across various patient populations. This condition is particularly concerning for frail elderly individuals, children with chronic illnesses, and critically ill patients. It often arises from inadequate nutrient intake, malabsorption, or increased metabolic demands due to conditions such as cancer, severe burns, and chronic diseases like cystic fibrosis and EPOC (chronic obstructive pulmonary disease).\n\nIn hospitalized patients, \"DESNUTRICI\u00d3N\" can complicate recovery and is often assessed through nutritional screening tools. It is prevalent among surgical patients, those with dysphagia, and individuals undergoing aggressive treatments, as inadequate nutrition can lead to weakened immune function, muscle wasting, and prolonged hospital stays. The condition can also affect the effectiveness of medications and is associated with various health issues, including complications like quilothorax and ascitic chylous.\n\n\"DESNUTRICI\u00d3N\" is recognized as a significant public health issue affecting both developing and developed countries, necessitating dietary assessment and intervention to prevent and treat malnutrition. Nutritional support, including enteral or parenteral nutrition, may be required for patients unable to meet their caloric needs through oral intake alone. The healthcare system aims to identify, prevent, and treat this condition to improve patient outcomes and quality of life."}{"title": "HOSPITAL:The hospital is a comprehensive healthcare institution that provides a wide range of medical treatments and care for patients with various conditions. It includes specialized services such as nutritional assessments and dietary management, which are critical for patient care. The hospital features a kitchen service that prepares meals tailored to the specific dietary needs of patients, including those requiring gluten-free diets, easy-to-chew diets, and pureed diets.\n\nPatients at the hospital receive treatment for numerous medical conditions, including acute pancreatitis, respiratory diseases like EPOC and cystic fibrosis, and neurodegenerative diseases such as Alzheimer's. The hospital is equipped to conduct medical procedures, including swallowing evaluations and the administration of parenteral nutrition, particularly for pediatric patients and those with eating disorders like anorexia nervosa (AN) and bulimia nervosa (BN).\n\nThe hospital also addresses the nutritional needs of patients with specific conditions, such as dysphagia, and implements protocols for managing complications like hyponatremia and hypocalcemia. It serves as a setting for various studies related to diabetes and malnutrition, ensuring that patients receive appropriate nutritional interventions.\n\nIn addition to medical treatment, the hospital provides training for families on enteral nutrition and offers multidisciplinary care for patients with complex needs, such as those with mitochondrial neurogastrointestinal encephalomyopathy (MNGIE). The hospital is a vital component of health management, focusing on improving the quality of care and attention for admitted patients, including those in critical condition or undergoing procedures like hematopoietic cell transplants.\n\nOverall, the hospital is dedicated to delivering comprehensive medical care, nutritional support, and specialized services to enhance patient outcomes and well-being."}{"title": "LUISA MAR\u00cdA ANDR\u00c9S ESTEBAN:Luisa Mar\u00eda Andr\u00e9s Esteban is a professional involved in the field of oropharyngeal dysphagia. She is a co-author of a manual that focuses on this condition, contributing to the development of multidisciplinary solutions aimed at addressing the challenges associated with dysphagia. In addition to her academic contributions, she works as a cook in the Hospital's Kitchen Service, specifically within the Functional Unit of Orofar\u00edngea Dysphagia, where she applies her expertise to support patients with this condition through appropriate dietary management."}{"title": "ROSA ANA ASHBAUGH ENGUIDANOS:Rosa Ana Ashbaugh Enguidanos is a dedicated professional specializing in nursing care for patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia. She works as a nurse in the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias, where her primary focus is on the treatment of dysphagia. In addition to her clinical work, Rosa Ana is also an author who contributes to the field of nutrition, particularly emphasizing the use of thickening agents in the management of dysphagia. Her expertise and contributions are significant in enhancing the care and nutritional support for patients facing these challenges."}{"title": "ELENA ATIENZA S\u00c1NCHEZ:Elena Atienza S\u00e1nchez is a Resident Intern Physician in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Section at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias. She is actively involved in research, particularly focusing on the role of digital technology in health and dysphagia. Additionally, she has contributed as a co-author to a section discussing oropharyngeal dysphagia in a relevant document. Furthermore, Elena is an author engaged in the study and documentation of nutritional practices specifically tailored for dysphagia patients."}{"title": "M\u00d3NICA BENITO FERN\u00c1NDEZ:M\u00f3nica Benito Fern\u00e1ndez is a dedicated professional in the field of nursing and nutrition, specifically focusing on the nutritional treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia. She is a nurse who graduated in Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics and currently works in the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias. In her role, she provides nursing care for patients suffering from oropharyngeal dysphagia, ensuring they receive appropriate nutritional support. Additionally, M\u00f3nica is a co-author of a document highlighting the importance of oral hygiene, further emphasizing her commitment to patient care and health education. Her research contributions are significant in enhancing the understanding and management of oropharyngeal dysphagia, showcasing her expertise and dedication to improving patient outcomes in this area."}{"title": "JULI\u00c1N FERN\u00c1NDEZ MAC\u00cdAS:Juli\u00e1n Fern\u00e1ndez Mac\u00edas is a multifaceted professional involved in the field of oropharyngeal dysphagia. He is a contributor to a manual that addresses this condition, specifically focusing on solutions applicable in hospital settings. In addition to his contributions to medical literature, he works as a cook in the Hospital's Kitchen Service, where he plays a vital role in the Functional Unit of Orofar\u00edngea Dysphagia. Furthermore, Juli\u00e1n is an author of recipes featured in Cocina Hospitalaria, showcasing his culinary expertise and commitment to enhancing the dietary options for patients with dysphagia. Through these roles, Juli\u00e1n Fern\u00e1ndez Mac\u00edas combines his knowledge of dysphagia with practical culinary skills to improve patient care in a hospital environment."}{"title": "PILAR GALLEGO IZQUIERDO:Pilar Gallego Izquierdo is a speech therapist working in the Rehabilitation Service at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias, where she specializes in dysphagia, particularly oropharyngeal dysphagia. She is a contributor to a manual that addresses solutions for oropharyngeal dysphagia, with a specific focus on exercises designed for orofacial structures that are crucial for the swallowing process. Additionally, Pilar Gallego Izquierdo is recognized as an author who has made significant contributions to the understanding of oropharyngeal dysphagia, enhancing the knowledge and resources available in this field."}{"title": "ELISA GARC\u00cdA GARC\u00cdA:Elisa Garc\u00eda Garc\u00eda is a Nursing Auxiliary Technician in the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias. In addition to her role in clinical nutrition, she is also a co-author of a manual on oropharyngeal dysphagia, which emphasizes dietary adaptations for patients suffering from this condition."}{"title": "ANTONIO GIL CORDERO:Antonio Gil Cordero is a prominent figure in the field of dietary management and culinary services within healthcare. He is a co-author of a manual on oropharyngeal dysphagia, which enhances the understanding of dietary needs for individuals with swallowing difficulties. Additionally, he has contributed recipes to \"Cocina Hospitalaria,\" showcasing his expertise in hospital cuisine. Currently, Antonio serves as the Head of Kitchen at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias, where he is responsible for managing food services for patients, ensuring that their dietary requirements are met with professionalism and care."}{"title": "NURIA GIL-FOURNIER ESQUERRA:Nuria Gil-Fournier Esquerra is a Specialist Physician in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Section at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias. She also practices at the Hospital General de Villalba in Madrid, where she specializes in endocrinology and nutrition. In addition to her clinical work, Nuria is a contributor to clinical guidelines on dysphagia, indicating her expertise in this area, which is closely related to otolaryngology. She works in the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar\u00edngea, where she is actively involved in the treatment of patients with dysphagia. Furthermore, Nuria is a researcher focused on dysphagia screening methods and clinical assessments, and she explores the intersection of internet technology and health, particularly in relation to dysphagia."}{"title": "CARMEN G\u00d3MEZ TRIGUERO:Carmen G\u00f3mez Triguero is a Specialist Physician in the Rehabilitation Service at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias. She is actively involved in research concerning oropharyngeal dysphagia rehabilitation, contributing as a co-author to various studies in this field. Additionally, she has played a significant role in developing a manual that addresses solutions for oropharyngeal dysphagia, with a particular focus on exercises designed for orofacial structures that are crucial for the swallowing process. Through her work, Carmen G\u00f3mez Triguero has established herself as a key contributor to the understanding and treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia."}{"title": "MONTSERRAT MART\u00cdNEZ LI\u00c9BANA:Montserrat Mart\u00ednez Li\u00e9bana is a Senior Technician in Dietetics and Nutrition at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias."}{"title": "LOURDES MONEVA VICENTE:Lourdes Moneva Vicente is a dedicated nurse in the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias. She specializes in the nutritional treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia, providing essential nursing care for patients affected by this condition. In addition to her clinical work, Lourdes is also a co-author of a document that emphasizes the importance of oral hygiene, highlighting her commitment to improving patient care and outcomes in her field."}{"title": "NATASHA P\u00c9REZ MARRERO:Natasha P\u00e9rez Marrero is a Specialist Physician in the Otolaryngology Service at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias. She is recognized for her contributions to the clinical guidelines on dysphagia, indicating her expertise in the field of otolaryngology."}{"title": "TERESA RIVERA RODR\u00cdGUEZ:Teresa Rivera Rodr\u00edguez is a prominent figure in the field of otolaryngology, serving as the Head of the Otolaryngology Service at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias. In addition to her leadership role, she is also an Associate Professor of Health Sciences. Her expertise is further demonstrated through her contributions to clinical guidelines on dysphagia, indicating her significant involvement and knowledge in this specialized area of medicine."}{"title": "MANUAL DE DISFAGIA OROFAR\u00cdNGEA:The \"Manual de Disfagia Orofaringea\" is a comprehensive guide designed to address oropharyngeal dysphagia through a multidisciplinary approach. It offers a wide range of solutions for the assessment, diagnosis, and treatment of this swallowing disorder, focusing on various aspects such as hydration, nutritional therapy, dietary adaptations, and rehabilitation strategies.\n\nThe manual includes detailed information on diagnostic scales and evaluation techniques for swallowing disorders, as well as clinical history considerations, gastrointestinal symptoms, and functional capacity assessments. It emphasizes the importance of tailored dietary recommendations, including texture modifications and liquid viscosities, to meet the nutritional needs of individuals with oropharyngeal dysphagia.\n\nIn addition to dietary guidelines, the manual provides practical solutions such as recipes and cooking techniques specifically designed for patients with swallowing difficulties. It also discusses exercises and techniques aimed at improving muscle strength and swallowing function, particularly for those affected by neurological conditions, head and neck cancer, or post-stroke recovery.\n\nFurthermore, the \"Manual de Disfagia Orofaringea\" addresses safety protocols in food preparation, allergen management, and oral hygiene practices, ensuring comprehensive care for patients. It serves as a valuable resource for healthcare professionals and caregivers involved in the management of oropharyngeal dysphagia, particularly in elderly patients and those with complex medical needs."}{"title": "VIRGINIA RODR\u00cdGUEZ CAMPUZANO:Virginia Rodr\u00edguez Campuzano is a dedicated nurse in the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias, where she specializes in the care of patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia. In her role, she is actively involved in providing nursing care tailored to the needs of these patients. Additionally, Virginia has contributed to the field through her research on multidisciplinary solutions for oropharyngeal dysphagia, highlighting her commitment to advancing knowledge and practices in this area. She is also a co-author of a document emphasizing the importance of oral hygiene, further showcasing her dedication to improving patient care and health outcomes."}{"title": "MANUEL RODR\u00cdGUEZ PARADINAS:Manuel Rodr\u00edguez Paradinas is a prominent figure in the field of oropharyngeal dysphagia rehabilitation, serving as a co-author and contributor to clinical guidelines related to dysphagia. He is recognized as an expert in otolaryngology and plays a vital role in the multidisciplinary team at the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar\u00edngea. His research interests include studying the impact of digital technology on health and dysphagia, highlighting his commitment to advancing knowledge in this area. Additionally, he specializes in the Otolaryngology Service and is responsible for overseeing the Oropharyngeal Dysphagia Functional Unit at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias. Through his work, Manuel Rodr\u00edguez Paradinas focuses on the treatment and evaluation of oropharyngeal dysphagia, contributing significantly to the understanding and management of this condition."}{"title": "PAULA ROMERO CORT\u00c9S:Paula Romero Cort\u00e9s is a medical resident specializing in Endocrinology and Nutrition at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias. In addition to her clinical training, she is also an author who contributes to the understanding of nutritional support for patients with dysphagia, highlighting her commitment to improving patient care through both practice and research."}{"title": "MAR\u00cdA DOLORES VALVERDE CARRILLO:Mar\u00eda Dolores Valverde Carrillo is a prominent figure in the field of oropharyngeal dysphagia, contributing significantly to both research and clinical practice. She is a member of the team at the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar\u00edngea, where she focuses on patient care and rehabilitation. As the head of the Rehabilitation Service and an associate professor of Health Sciences at the University of Alcal\u00e1 (UAH), she plays a crucial role in the study and treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia.\n\nHer contributions include authoring a manual on oropharyngeal dysphagia solutions, which emphasizes exercises for orofacial structures essential for swallowing. Additionally, she is involved in research that examines the effects of internet and digital technology on health and dysphagia, further expanding the understanding of this condition and its impact on quality of life. Through her work, Mar\u00eda Dolores Valverde Carrillo is dedicated to advancing the knowledge and treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia, making her a key contributor to the field."}{"title": "DYSFAGIA OROFAR\u00cdNGEA:Dysfagia Orofaringea, or oropharyngeal dysphagia, is a condition that impacts the swallowing process, particularly affecting the throat. This specific type of dysphagia is a significant focus of clinical study and treatment at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias. Various screening methods are employed to assess oropharyngeal dysphagia, highlighting its importance in clinical settings."}{"title": "MADRID:Madrid is the capital city of Spain and serves as a significant political, economic, and cultural center. It is home to various important institutions, including the Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n, which is dedicated to research and publications in the fields of endocrinology and nutrition. This society has published numerous significant works, including the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n\" and the \"Tratado de Nutrici\u00f3n,\" as well as the 3rd edition of the pediatric gastroenterology, hepatology, and nutrition treatment guidelines.\n\nIn addition to its role in medical publishing, Madrid is also noted for its healthcare infrastructure, housing several prominent hospitals such as the Hospital General Universitario Gregorio Mara\u00f1\u00f3n and Hospital Universitario 12 de Octubre. The city is involved in various healthcare initiatives, including the requirement for patients to submit justification reports to primary care centers for continued treatment related to nutritional needs.\n\nMadrid is recognized as a key location for medical literature, with significant contributions from publishing houses like Editorial M\u00e9dica Panamericana, S.A., which focuses on clinical nutrition. The city has also been a site for research related to oropharyngeal dysphagia and has reported on health issues such as the mortality rate for chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD).\n\nOverall, Madrid stands out as a central hub for advancements in nutrition and endocrinology, contributing to both national and international medical knowledge and practices."}{"title": "FISIOLOG\u00cdA DE LA DEGLUCI\u00d3N:The study of the physiological processes involved in swallowing, including the coordination of muscles and nerves."}{"title": "LANCASTER:An author who has defined dysphagia and contributed to the understanding of swallowing disorders."}{"title": "EVIDENCIA CIENT\u00cdFICA:EVIDENCIA CIENT\u00cdFICA refers to the quality and strength of evidence in scientific studies, which is classified into different levels. This concept encompasses a broad range of information that supports various fields, including the understanding and treatment of dysphagia, as well as clinical practices in nutrition. Overall, EVIDENCIA CIENT\u00cdFICA serves as a critical foundation for informed decision-making in scientific research and clinical applications."}{"title": "MORBIMORTALIDAD:MORBIMORTALIDAD refers to the frequency and incidence of diseases and deaths within a population, particularly in relation to various health conditions and factors such as malnutrition, surgical procedures, and specific patient demographics. It is a significant public health issue, especially concerning the impact of malnutrition on morbidity and mortality rates among vulnerable groups, including the elderly and critically ill patients. \n\nThe term encompasses the complications and mortality associated with medical conditions, including but not limited to oropharyngeal dysphagia, chronic respiratory diseases, and conditions like hyponatremia and cystic fibrosis. It is also relevant in evaluating health outcomes in patients undergoing surgical interventions, where it can be influenced by factors such as glycemic control. \n\nMORBIMORTALIDAD is particularly important in the context of cancer treatment, where it serves as a critical measure of patient outcomes. Overall, it highlights the interconnectedness of nutritional status and health, emphasizing the need for early detection and treatment of underlying health issues to mitigate the risks associated with morbidity and mortality."}{"title": "TRASTORNOS DEL \u00c1NIMO:Mood disorders are psychological impacts that can arise from the challenges faced by individuals with dysphagia."}{"title": "AISLAMIENTO:AISLAMIENTO refers to the phenomenon of isolation, which is a prevalent issue particularly among the elderly population. This isolation can have detrimental effects on their nutritional habits, as social interactions are often linked to eating and meal preparation. Additionally, isolation serves as a social consequence that can significantly impact patients suffering from dysphagia, a condition characterized by difficulties in swallowing. For these individuals, the challenges associated with eating can be exacerbated by a lack of social support and interaction, further complicating their nutritional intake and overall well-being."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N:\"Alimentaci\u00f3n\" encompasses a broad range of dietary management strategies and practices essential for maintaining health and nutritional status across various patient populations. It refers to the act of eating, which is closely linked to swallowing processes that can be impacted by conditions such as dysphagia. In the context of healthcare, alimentaci\u00f3n involves dietary aspects and nutritional care provided to patients during hospitalization, ensuring that their dietary intake is adequate, whether it is normal or deteriorated.\n\nFor patients with specific health conditions, such as pancreatitis or head and neck cancers, alimentaci\u00f3n plays a critical role in alleviating symptoms and providing necessary nutritional support. It also includes the assessment of eating habits through tools like the Mini Nutritional Assessment, which evaluates nutritional intake and overall health.\n\nFurthermore, alimentaci\u00f3n addresses the feeding practices and nutritional strategies vital for the health and growth of infants, particularly those who are preterm. It emphasizes the importance of hydration and nutrient intake, which are crucial for maintaining physical performance and overall well-being.\n\nIn summary, alimentaci\u00f3n is a multifaceted concept that involves the careful planning, preparation, and provision of food and hydration tailored to meet the needs of individuals, particularly those facing health challenges, ensuring their safety and promoting optimal health outcomes."}{"title": "DEGLUCI\u00d3N:\"DEGLUCI\u00d3n\" refers to the process of swallowing, which involves the formation and movement of a food bolus through the digestive system. This act, known as deglutition, is critical for individuals, particularly those with swallowing difficulties, such as patients with head and neck cancers, multiple sclerosis, or those who have experienced a stroke. Swallowing can be impaired by various medical conditions, necessitating regular assessments and specific exercises to improve the function. In the context of dysphagia, the act of swallowing is actively engaged in during treatment, and it can be enhanced through the use of thickeners to ensure safety for individuals facing these challenges. The process of degluci\u00f3n encompasses multiple phases and mechanisms, highlighting its complexity and the importance of understanding its implications for affected patients."}{"title": "NERVIO VAGO:El nervio vago es un nervio craneal que proporciona inervaci\u00f3n sensorial y motora a los m\u00fasculos involucrados en la degluci\u00f3n y el tracto respiratorio superior."}{"title": "C\u00d3RTEX:El c\u00f3rtex es la parte del cerebro que participa en el control neural de la degluci\u00f3n, coordinando los procesos motores necesarios para este evento."}{"title": "BOLLO ALIMENTICIO:The \"BOLLO ALIMENTICIO\" refers to the mass of food that is formed in the mouth during the process of swallowing. This mass is created as food is chewed and mixed with saliva, and it is then transferred to the esophagus. The bolo alimenticio plays a crucial role in the digestive process, facilitating the movement of food from the mouth to the esophagus for further digestion."}{"title": "M\u00daSCULOS INFRAHIOIDEOS:Los m\u00fasculos infrahioideos ayudan a la recuperaci\u00f3n de la configuraci\u00f3n respiratoria despu\u00e9s de la degluci\u00f3n."}{"title": "TRIG\u00c9MINO:El nervio trig\u00e9mino es un nervio craneal que participa en la masticaci\u00f3n y en la motilidad de labios y mejillas durante la degluci\u00f3n."}{"title": "FACIAL:El nervio facial es un nervio craneal que tambi\u00e9n participa en la motilidad de labios y mejillas durante la degluci\u00f3n."}{"title": "GLOSOFAR\u00cdNGEO:El nervio glosofar\u00edngeo es un nervio craneal que participa en la degluci\u00f3n, proporcionando inervaci\u00f3n a la faringe."}{"title": "HIPOGLOSO:El nervio hipogloso es un nervio craneal que inerva la lengua, facilitando su movimiento durante la degluci\u00f3n."}{"title": "ES\u00d3FAGO:The es\u00f3fago, or esophagus, is a muscular tube that plays a crucial role in the digestive system by transporting the bolus of food from the pharynx to the stomach during the process of swallowing. It is essential for the proper movement of food, and its function can be impacted by various swallowing disorders."}{"title": "LARINGE:La laringe es una parte fundamental del tracto respiratorio que desempe\u00f1a un papel crucial durante la degluci\u00f3n, ya que se cierra para evitar que el bolo alimenticio ingrese a las v\u00edas respiratorias. Adem\u00e1s, la laringe es una estructura anat\u00f3mica que se eval\u00faa durante la evaluaci\u00f3n de la degluci\u00f3n (VED) debido a su importancia en este proceso. Su funci\u00f3n en la degluci\u00f3n puede verse afectada por diversas condiciones que pueden llevar a la disfagia, un trastorno que dificulta la capacidad de tragar."}{"title": "EPIGLOTIS:La epiglotis es una estructura que bloquea la laringe durante la degluci\u00f3n, asegurando que el bolo alimenticio se dirija al es\u00f3fago."}{"title": "PALADAR:El paladar es la parte superior de la boca que ayuda a cerrar la cavidad nasal durante la degluci\u00f3n."}{"title": "NERVIOS CRANEALES:Los nervios craneales son un grupo de nervios que proporcionan la inervaci\u00f3n necesaria para los m\u00fasculos involucrados en la degluci\u00f3n."}{"title": "FARINGE:The entity \"FARINGE,\" also known as the pharynx, is a critical anatomical structure involved in the swallowing process. It is a muscular tube that connects the mouth and nasal passages to the esophagus, playing a vital role in the act of swallowing. The pharynx is assessed during procedures such as video fluoroscopy and VED (Videofluoroscopic Evaluation of Swallowing), highlighting its importance in evaluating swallowing function. Overall, the pharynx is an essential part of the throat that facilitates the transition of food and air, underscoring its significance in both respiratory and digestive systems."}{"title": "N\u00daCLEO DEL TRACTO SOLITARIO:El n\u00facleo del tracto solitario es una estructura en el sistema nervioso central que juega un papel crucial en la degluci\u00f3n y la integraci\u00f3n de informaci\u00f3n sensorial relacionada con este proceso."}{"title": "CEREBRO:CEREBRO refers to the brain, a central organ of the nervous system that plays a crucial role in regulating various functions, including swallowing and respiration. It is significantly impacted in patients with adrenoleukodystrophy due to inflammatory responses. Additionally, the brain is involved in various biochemical processes, including those related to copper metabolism. In the context of Wilson's disease, the brain is another critical organ affected, as copper accumulation can lead to neurological symptoms. Overall, CEREBRO encompasses the complex functions and vulnerabilities of the brain in relation to different medical conditions."}{"title": "ACCIDENTE CEREBROVASCULAR:A cerebrovascular accident (commonly known as a stroke) is a medical event that can significantly impact a person's ability to swallow, a condition known as dysphagia. This occurs due to damage to the brain areas responsible for swallowing, which is a direct result of interrupted blood flow to the brain. As a consequence of dysphagia, patients who have experienced a cerebrovascular accident are at an increased risk of developing aspiration pneumonia, a serious complication that arises when food or liquid enters the lungs."}{"title": "RESONANCIA MAGN\u00c9TICA:Resonancia Magn\u00e9tica, or Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI), is a non-invasive diagnostic technique utilized for various medical purposes. It is primarily known for its application in studying brain activity and its relationship with functions such as swallowing and other neurological processes. Additionally, MRI serves as an important tool for quantifying liver iron concentration and assessing liver damage, particularly in patients suffering from hereditary hemochromatosis. This versatility highlights the significance of Resonancia Magn\u00e9tica in both neurological and hepatic evaluations."}{"title": "ESTIMULACI\u00d3N MAGN\u00c9TICA TRANSCRANEAL:La estimulaci\u00f3n magn\u00e9tica transcraneal es una t\u00e9cnica que permite investigar la funci\u00f3n cerebral y su implicaci\u00f3n en procesos como la degluci\u00f3n."}{"title": "FORMACI\u00d3N RETICULAR:La formaci\u00f3n reticular es una estructura en el tronco del enc\u00e9falo que juega un papel importante en la regulaci\u00f3n de la degluci\u00f3n y la respiraci\u00f3n."}{"title": "GANGLIOS BASALES:Los ganglios basales son un grupo de n\u00facleos en el cerebro que est\u00e1n implicados en el control motor y pueden influir en la degluci\u00f3n."}{"title": "T\u00c1LAMO:El t\u00e1lamo es una estructura cerebral que forma parte del sistema nervioso central y act\u00faa como un centro de relevo para la informaci\u00f3n sensorial. Adem\u00e1s de su funci\u00f3n en el procesamiento sensorial, el t\u00e1lamo est\u00e1 involucrado en la regulaci\u00f3n de la alimentaci\u00f3n y la degluci\u00f3n, especialmente en los ni\u00f1os. Su papel es crucial en la integraci\u00f3n de diversas se\u00f1ales que afectan estas funciones vitales."}{"title": "CEREBELO:El cerebelo es una parte del cerebro que coordina el movimiento y puede influir en la funci\u00f3n de degluci\u00f3n."}{"title": "CORTEX CEREBRAL:La corteza cerebral es una parte fundamental del sistema nervioso central, responsable de diversas funciones cognitivas y motoras. Estas funciones son cruciales para el desarrollo conductual en los ni\u00f1os, as\u00ed como para procesos relacionados con la alimentaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "ACIDENTE CEREBROVASCULAR:El accidente cerebrovascular es un evento m\u00e9dico que afecta la funci\u00f3n neurol\u00f3gica y puede causar disfagia debido a la p\u00e9rdida de conectividad funcional en la red de degluci\u00f3n."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE PARKINSON:The \"ENFERMEDAD DE PARKINSON,\" or Parkinson's disease, is a neurodegenerative disorder that primarily affects motor control, leading to difficulties in movement and coordination. This condition can significantly impact various bodily functions, including the ability to interrupt the vagal tone of the esophagus, which is crucial for swallowing. As a result, individuals with Parkinson's disease often experience a high prevalence of swallowing disorders, known as dysphagia, which can increase the risk of malnutrition. Due to these challenges, patients may require nutritional support and specific screening and treatment recommendations to manage their symptoms effectively. Overall, Parkinson's disease is characterized by its profound effects on motor functions and the associated risks of complications related to swallowing and nutrition."}{"title": "P. CLAV\u00c9:P. Clav\u00e9 is a researcher who has focused on the study of swallowing and has developed methods for evaluating the propulsion forces of the tongue."}{"title": "ESCLEROSIS LATERAL AMIOTR\u00d3FICA:Esclerosis lateral amiotr\u00f3fica (ELA), also known as amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS), is a progressive neurodegenerative disease that primarily affects motor neurons. This degeneration leads to significant muscle weakness and can result in dysphagia, or swallowing difficulties, which occur in approximately 60% of patients. As the disease progresses, individuals may experience increased risks of malnutrition due to these swallowing challenges, necessitating specific nutritional interventions and targeted care strategies. The condition is characterized by the gradual loss of motor function, which can ultimately lead to paralysis. Overall, ELA is a complex disease that requires comprehensive management to address both its neurological and nutritional implications."}{"title": "ATROFIA MUSCULAR BULBOESPINAL:La atrofia muscular bulboespinal es una condici\u00f3n que causa lesiones en las motoneuronas y afecta la funci\u00f3n de degluci\u00f3n."}{"title": "PLASTICIDAD NEURONAL:La plasticidad neuronal se refiere a la capacidad del cerebro para reorganizarse y adaptarse, lo que es crucial para la recuperaci\u00f3n funcional despu\u00e9s de un accidente cerebrovascular."}{"title": "NEUROANATOM\u00cdA:"}{"title": "EES:The upper esophageal sphincter (EES) is a crucial muscular structure that facilitates the opening during the swallowing process, allowing food to pass from the pharynx to the esophagus. It plays a significant role in the swallowing mechanism and can be impacted by various medical conditions, particularly in cases of dysphagia oropharyngeal. The EES is essential for proper swallowing function, and any dysfunction in this area can lead to swallowing disorders."}{"title": "P. CALV\u00c9:P. Calv\u00e9 es un autor que ha defendido el uso de videofluoroscopia para analizar la respuesta motora orofar\u00edngea y la apertura del EES."}{"title": "DIVERT\u00cdCULO DE ZENKER:The \"Divert\u00edculo de Zenker\" is a structural issue characterized by the formation of a pharyngeal pouch, which can lead to various swallowing symptoms that are influenced by the size of the diverticulum. This condition is associated with fibrosis of the upper esophageal sphincter (EES), which can affect its distensibility. As a result, individuals with Zenker's diverticulum may experience difficulties in swallowing, making it an important esophageal condition to recognize and address."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE CROHN:Enfermedad de Crohn, tambi\u00e9n conocida como Crohn's disease (CD), es un tipo de enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal (EII) que puede afectar cualquier segmento del tracto gastrointestinal, desde la boca hasta el ano. Esta enfermedad se caracteriza por una inflamaci\u00f3n discontinua que afecta todas las capas de la pared intestinal, lo que puede llevar a una variedad de s\u00edntomas, incluyendo dolor abdominal, diarrea severa, fatiga, p\u00e9rdida de peso y malnutrici\u00f3n. \n\nLa enfermedad de Crohn es cr\u00f3nica y puede presentar complicaciones como malabsorci\u00f3n de nutrientes, incluyendo la vitamina E, y dificultades para tragar. Adem\u00e1s, puede causar problemas en la apertura del esf\u00ednter esof\u00e1gico superior (EES) y tr\u00e1nsito intestinal lento, a menudo asociado con el s\u00edndrome de intestino corto. Debido a la naturaleza de la enfermedad, muchos pacientes, especialmente en la poblaci\u00f3n pedi\u00e1trica, pueden requerir nutrici\u00f3n enteral como parte de su manejo para controlar los s\u00edntomas y prevenir la desnutrici\u00f3n. \n\nEn resumen, la enfermedad de Crohn es un trastorno inflamatorio intestinal que provoca una serie de s\u00edntomas gastrointestinales y puede tener un impacto significativo en la calidad de vida de quienes la padecen."}{"title": "MIOPAT\u00cdA POR CUERPOS DE INCLUSI\u00d3N:La miopat\u00eda por cuerpos de inclusi\u00f3n es una condici\u00f3n que puede estar relacionada con la disfunci\u00f3n del EES."}{"title": "MANOMETR\u00cdA:MANOMETR\u00cdA is a functional diagnostic test utilized to evaluate the pressure and distensibility of the esophageal sphincter (EES) during the act of swallowing. This technique is particularly important for assessing esophageal motility disorders and swallowing function in patients experiencing oropharyngeal dysphagia. By measuring the pressure and patterns of muscle contractions in the esophagus, manometr\u00eda provides critical insights into the underlying neural or muscular mechanisms, helping to differentiate between primary esophageal obstruction and mechanical obstruction. Often, this procedure is performed alongside impedance testing to enhance diagnostic accuracy."}{"title": "RESIDUOS POSTDEGLUCI\u00d3N:Los residuos postdegluci\u00f3n son restos de alimento que pueden quedar en la faringe despu\u00e9s de tragar, lo que puede indicar problemas en la apertura del EES."}{"title": "ASPIRACI\u00d3N:Aspiration, referred to as \"ASPIRACI\u00d3N,\" occurs when material enters the airway below the vocal cords, which poses a significant risk of respiratory complications. This condition is particularly associated with an abnormal opening of the upper esophageal sphincter (EES), where food can inadvertently enter the respiratory tract, increasing the likelihood of respiratory issues."}{"title": "M\u00daSCULOS SUPRAHIOIDEOS:"}{"title": "MIOSITIS POR CUERPOS DE INCLUSI\u00d3N:Inclusion body myositis is a muscle disorder that can lead to swallowing difficulties due to muscle weakness."}{"title": "EJERCICIO SHAKER:The Shaker exercise is a rehabilitation technique aimed at improving swallowing function by strengthening the suprahyoid muscles."}{"title": "MANIOBRA DE MENDELSOHN:The \"MANIOBRA DE MENDELSOHN,\" also known as the Mendelsohn maneuver, is a specialized technique designed to enhance the swallowing process. This maneuver focuses on prolonging the elevation of the larynx during swallowing, which serves to improve airway protection and minimize pharyngeal residue. Additionally, it aims to improve the coordination of swallowing and the function of the upper esophageal sphincter (EES). Overall, the Mendelsohn maneuver is an effective strategy for individuals experiencing swallowing difficulties, contributing to safer and more efficient swallowing."}{"title": "LESIONES POSTQUIR\u00daRGICAS:Post-surgical injuries can lead to complications affecting swallowing, resulting in oropharyngeal dysphagia."}{"title": "TRAUMATISMOS CRANEOENCEF\u00c1LICOS:Head injuries can disrupt the neural pathways involved in swallowing, leading to dysphagia."}{"title": "DEMENCIA:Dementia is a cognitive disorder that primarily affects cognitive functions, often associated with aging and cognitive frailty. It can lead to various complications, one of which is oropharyngeal dysphagia, a condition that impairs the ability to swallow. This impairment is particularly significant in older adults, as dementia can contribute to the development of dysphagia, further complicating their health and care needs."}{"title": "ESCLEROSIS M\u00daLTIPLE:Esclerosis m\u00faltiple, or multiple sclerosis (MS), is a chronic neurological disease that affects the central nervous system, leading to a variety of neurological symptoms. It is characterized by its impact on muscle control, which can result in dysphagia (swallowing difficulties) in approximately 60% of patients. This condition not only contributes to challenges in swallowing but also increases the risk of malnutrition among affected individuals. As a result, managing esclerosis m\u00faltiple requires specific nutritional guidelines to enhance the well-being of patients. Additionally, esclerosis m\u00faltiple is recognized as one of the 17 thematic research networks under RETICS, emphasizing its significance in ongoing medical research and treatment strategies."}{"title": "POLIOMIELITIS:Poliomyelitis is a viral disease that can cause paralysis and affect swallowing muscles, leading to dysphagia."}{"title": "PAR\u00c1LISIS CEREBRAL:Cerebral palsy, known as \"PAR\u00c1LISIS CEREBRAL,\" is a group of disorders that primarily affect movement and muscle tone. Individuals with cerebral palsy may experience a range of challenges, including severe difficulties with swallowing. These swallowing difficulties can be significant enough to necessitate enteral nutrition for those affected, highlighting the impact of the condition on daily functioning and health."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE GUILLAIN-BARR\u00c9:Guillain-Barr\u00e9 syndrome is a neurological autoimmune disorder characterized by muscle weakness and can significantly impact various bodily functions, including swallowing. In some cases, the severity of the condition may require patients to rely on enteral nutrition to meet their dietary needs."}{"title": "COREA DE HUNTINGTON:Huntington's disease is a genetic disorder that can lead to movement and cognitive issues, including difficulties with swallowing."}{"title": "TRASTORNOS CONG\u00c9NITOS O DEGENERATIVOS CEREBRALES:Congenital or degenerative brain disorders can impact swallowing function, leading to dysphagia."}{"title": "DIABETES MELLITUS:Diabetes Mellitus (DM) is a chronic metabolic disorder characterized by high blood sugar levels due to the body's inability to effectively process glucose. This condition can arise from insulin resistance or insufficient insulin production and is associated with various health complications if not managed properly. Diabetes Mellitus is prevalent in different populations, including those with specific health conditions such as cancer, chronic pancreatitis, and MELAS syndrome, and it often coexists with other clinical issues, complicating their management.\n\nThe management of Diabetes Mellitus requires careful dietary considerations, lifestyle changes, and sometimes medication, including insulin therapy. Nutritional support is particularly important for hospitalized patients and those with comorbidities, as diabetes can influence dietary management and nutritional needs. For instance, dietary fat intake, glycemic index, and the consumption of fruits and vegetables can significantly impact blood sugar control. Additionally, diabetes is a significant risk factor for malnutrition, especially in elderly patients and those with chronic illnesses.\n\nDiabetes Mellitus can lead to serious complications, including hypoglycemia, diabetic ketoacidosis, chronic kidney disease, and cognitive decline, including dementia. It is also linked to conditions such as sarcopenia and can complicate medical procedures. The condition is increasingly recognized as a public health issue, necessitating coordinated efforts for prevention and control due to its rising prevalence and associated health complications globally.\n\nIn summary, Diabetes Mellitus is a complex chronic condition that requires comprehensive management strategies, including dietary management, lifestyle modifications, and medical interventions, to maintain health and prevent complications."}{"title": "ALCOHOLISMO CR\u00d3NICO:Chronic alcoholism, referred to as \"ALCOHOLISMO CR\u00d3NICO,\" is a serious condition that can lead to various health complications. It is known to cause neurological damage, which can impair an individual's ability to swallow. Additionally, chronic alcoholism is a major contributor to liver disease; however, it is noteworthy that only 15% of individuals suffering from chronic alcoholism progress to advanced liver disease. Furthermore, chronic alcoholism is identified as the most prevalent cause of chronic pancreatitis in adults, significantly heightening the risk of developing this condition. Overall, chronic alcoholism poses substantial health risks, affecting multiple organ systems and leading to severe medical issues."}{"title": "PAR\u00c1LISIS DEL NERVIO LAR\u00cdNGEO RECURRENTE:Recurrent laryngeal nerve paralysis can affect the muscles involved in swallowing, leading to dysphagia."}{"title": "NEOPLASIAS:NEOPLASIAS refer to abnormal growths of tissue that can manifest in various forms and lead to a range of medical complications. These growths can cause significant issues such as intestinal obstruction and malnutrition, often necessitating nutritional support through parenteral nutrition. Additionally, neoplasias can result in conditions like ascitis quilosa and quilot\u00f3rax, which are associated with fluid accumulation in the body. Tumors located in the throat or esophagus can obstruct swallowing, leading to dysphagia, and may require interventions such as gastrostomy for nutritional support. Furthermore, dietary factors can influence the development of neoplasms, which are recognized as a significant cause of mortality worldwide. Overall, neoplasias represent a serious health concern due to their potential to disrupt normal bodily functions and contribute to severe health complications."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE TAGLE:Tagle syndrome can involve neurological issues that affect swallowing."}{"title": "NEURALGIA DEL NERVIO GLOSOFAR\u00cdNGEO:Glossopharyngeal neuralgia can cause pain during swallowing, leading to avoidance and dysphagia."}{"title": "DIFTERIA:Diphtheria can cause throat swelling and complications that affect swallowing."}{"title": "T\u00c9TANOS:Tetanus can lead to muscle stiffness and spasms, affecting the ability to swallow."}{"title": "RABIA:Rabies can affect the nervous system and lead to swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "INTOXICACI\u00d3N POR PLOMO:Lead poisoning can cause neurological damage that affects swallowing."}{"title": "POLIMIOSITIS:Polymyositis is an inflammatory muscle disease that can lead to weakness and swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "DERMATOMIOSITIS:Dermatomyositis is an inflammatory condition that affects the skin and muscles, potentially leading to dysphagia."}{"title": "MIASTENIA GRAVIS:Myasthenia gravis is an autoimmune disorder that leads to muscle weakness, including the muscles involved in swallowing."}{"title": "ESCLEROSIS SIST\u00c9MICA PROGRESIVA:Progressive systemic sclerosis can affect muscle function and lead to swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE KEARNS-SAYRE:Kearns-Sayre syndrome is a mitochondrial disorder that can lead to muscle weakness and dysphagia."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE LAMBERT-EATON:Lambert-Eaton syndrome is a condition that affects the neuromuscular junction and can lead to swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "DISTROFIAS MUSCULARES:Muscular dystrophies are a group of genetic disorders that lead to muscle weakness and can affect swallowing."}{"title": "DISFUNCI\u00d3N TIROIDEA:Thyroid dysfunction, whether hyper- or hypothyroidism, can lead to muscle weakness affecting swallowing."}{"title": "CUERPO EXTRA\u00d1O:Foreign bodies in the throat can obstruct swallowing and lead to dysphagia."}{"title": "PROCESOS INFLAMATORIOS E INFECCIOSOS:Inflammatory and infectious processes, such as pharyngitis, can lead to swelling and dysphagia."}{"title": "MEMBRANA CRICOFAR\u00cdNGEA:Cricopharyngeal membrane can cause obstruction and lead to swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "MEMBRANAS ESOF\u00c1GICAS CERVICALES:Cervical esophageal membranes can obstruct swallowing and lead to dysphagia."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE PLUMMER-VINSON:Plummer-Vinson syndrome, also known as Sindrome de Plummer-Vinson, is a rare medical condition primarily associated with severe iron deficiency anemia. This syndrome is characterized by the formation of esophageal webs, which can lead to significant swallowing difficulties. The presence of these webs in the esophagus contributes to the challenges individuals face when consuming food, making it a notable aspect of the condition."}{"title": "BOCIO:Bocio, also known as goiter, is an enlargement of the thyroid gland that can arise from various thyroid disorders, including congenital hypothyroidism. This condition can lead to complications such as pressure on the esophagus, resulting in difficulties with swallowing."}{"title": "GRANDES OSTEOFITOS DE LA COLUMNA CERVICAL:Large cervical osteophytes can compress the esophagus and lead to dysphagia."}{"title": "LINFADENOPAT\u00cdA:Lymphadenopathy can cause pressure on the esophagus, leading to swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "NEOPLASIAS DE LA CAVIDAD ORAL:Neoplasms in the oral cavity can obstruct swallowing and lead to dysphagia."}{"title": "CAVIDAD ORAL:CAVIDAD ORAL, or the oral cavity, is the anatomical space within the mouth that encompasses the tongue, teeth, and gums. This area plays a crucial role in oral hygiene and health, making it significant in discussions related to these topics. The oral cavity is particularly important for hygiene practices, especially in patients receiving enteral nutrition, as it can influence their overall health and well-being. Additionally, the oral cavity serves as the initial part of the digestive system, where the process of swallowing begins. It is also a region where various sensory stimuli can be applied, which can modify aspects of swallowing, highlighting its functional importance in both digestion and sensory perception."}{"title": "PRESBIFAGIA:The term used to describe the effects of aging on swallowing functionality, including physiological changes that increase susceptibility to dysphagia."}{"title": "PACIENTE MAYOR Y MAYOR-MAYOR:Refers to elderly patients, particularly those over 70 years old, who are more susceptible to oropharyngeal dysphagia."}{"title": "SARCOPENIA:Sarcopenia is a condition characterized by the progressive loss of muscle mass and strength, primarily affecting older adults. This condition is significantly associated with aging and is linked to various health complications, including frailty, increased vulnerability to infections, and a higher risk of disability and mortality. Sarcopenia can also exacerbate health issues in patients with chronic diseases, such as cancer and liver cirrhosis, where it is often related to malnutrition and can impact overall prognosis.\n\nThe condition is particularly concerning in the elderly, as it contributes to functional decline and can lead to increased dependence and fragility. It is also associated with dysphagia, which affects swallowing ability, further complicating the health of older individuals. Nutritional interventions, including increased protein intake and exercise, have been shown to mitigate the effects of sarcopenia, highlighting the importance of proper nutrition and physical activity in managing this condition.\n\nSarcopenia was first proposed by Irwin Rosenberg in 1989 and has since been the focus of numerous studies aimed at understanding its implications and developing effective interventions. It is recognized as a syndrome that not only impacts physical health but can also influence cognitive health and overall quality of life in the elderly population."}{"title": "DINAPENIA:DINAPENIA refers to a condition characterized by the loss of muscle strength, particularly in elderly patients. This condition can significantly contribute to dysphagia, which is the difficulty in swallowing. The impact of dinapenia on muscle strength not only affects overall physical capabilities but also poses challenges in the swallowing process for the elderly population."}{"title": "KRATOPENIA:A condition involving loss of muscle endurance in elderly patients, which can exacerbate dysphagia."}{"title": "F\u00c1RMACOS:F\u00e1rmacos, or drugs and medications, are substances utilized in the treatment of various medical conditions. They play a crucial role in clinical practice, particularly in their interactions with diet and nutrients, which can significantly affect their efficacy and absorption. F\u00e1rmacos may need to be administered to patients receiving enteral nutrition, necessitating specific guidelines to ensure proper delivery and effectiveness.\n\nCertain medications, such as antibiotics and laxatives, are commonly associated with gastrointestinal side effects, including diarrhea and constipation. Additionally, f\u00e1rmacos like somatostatin analogs are specifically used to manage dumping syndrome and its related symptoms. The gastrointestinal side effects of f\u00e1rmacos can vary widely, with some causing chronic diarrhea depending on their nature and usage.\n\nF\u00e1rmacos are also essential in the control of metabolic processes, particularly in patients with burns, where they assist in managing nutrimetabolic needs. Furthermore, these medications can interact with nutrients during nutritional therapy, potentially impacting treatment outcomes. They may also affect thermoregulation and hydration in athletes, highlighting the importance of understanding their interactions with dietary components.\n\nMoreover, certain medications can interfere with swallowing functionality, especially in the elderly, and can disrupt the absorption and metabolism of thyroid hormones, which may compromise treatment efficacy. Overall, f\u00e1rmacos encompass a wide range of medications that require careful consideration of their interactions with diet and nutrients to optimize patient care."}{"title": "DOF:DOF, or Dysphagia Orofar\u00edngea, refers to a clinical condition characterized by difficulty in swallowing, which can significantly impact patients' health and quality of life. This condition is often associated with various medical issues and is particularly prevalent among the elderly. DOF requires a comprehensive and multidisciplinary management approach due to its implications for nutrition and hydration, as it can lead to malnutrition and dehydration.\n\nThe condition is recognized as a significant health concern, complicating the management of patients, especially those with comorbidities. It necessitates dietary modifications and the use of specific nutritional products to ensure safe consumption of food and liquids. Rehabilitation techniques and exercises may also be employed to improve swallowing function.\n\nFurthermore, DOF is linked to increased patient mortality, longer hospital stays, and higher healthcare costs, highlighting the need for specialized consultation services that address swallowing disorders. Despite its importance, there is a noted lack of such services across the country, indicating a gap in the healthcare system that needs to be addressed to better support affected individuals."}{"title": "ENVEJECIMIENTO:\"ENVEJECIMIENTO\" refers to the process of aging, a universal biological phenomenon that impacts individuals in diverse ways. This process leads to various physiological changes, including increased frailty and sarcopenia, which is characterized by a decline in muscle mass and strength. Aging significantly affects both cognitive function and nutritional needs, making it a critical factor in the overall health status of older adults. Additionally, it influences all aspects of health, including physical capabilities and the risk of conditions such as dysphagia. As the population of older adults continues to grow, understanding the implications of aging becomes increasingly important, as it is closely related to the deterioration of bodily systems and the overall well-being of the elderly."}{"title": "MASA MUSCULAR:Masa Muscular se refiere a la cantidad de tejido muscular presente en el cuerpo, un componente esencial para el rendimiento f\u00edsico y la salud de un deportista. Esta masa muscular puede ser evaluada mediante el \u00cdndice Creatinina-Altura, que proporciona una medida de la cantidad de m\u00fasculo en relaci\u00f3n con la altura de una persona. Adem\u00e1s, es importante destacar que la masa muscular tiende a disminuir con el envejecimiento, lo que puede tener implicaciones en la salud, incluyendo condiciones como la disfagia. En resumen, la masa muscular es un indicador clave de la salud f\u00edsica y el bienestar general, especialmente en el contexto del deporte y el envejecimiento."}{"title": "FUNCIONALIDAD DE LA DEGLUCI\u00d3N:The ability to swallow effectively, which can be impaired in elderly patients due to various factors."}{"title": "CABR\u00c9 ET AL:Cabr\u00e9 et al are researchers who studied the characteristics of elderly patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "NEUMON\u00cdAS DE REPETICI\u00d3N:Recurrent pneumonia is a common complication in patients with dysphagia, particularly those with degenerative neurological diseases."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME GERI\u00c1TRICO:Geriatric syndrome refers to a group of conditions that commonly affect older adults, including dysphagia, stroke, and dementia."}{"title": "ICTUS:ICTUS refers to a stroke, a significant medical event characterized by the interruption of blood supply to the brain. This condition is particularly prevalent among the elderly and women, making it the second leading cause of death in Spain. A stroke can lead to various complications, including dysphagia, which is a severe swallowing difficulty that may necessitate targeted rehabilitation exercises to improve tongue strength and swallowing function. \n\nPatients who experience an ictus often face oropharyngeal dysphagia, which increases the risk of aspiration pneumonia and mortality, especially in those with dysphagia. Early screening and treatment are crucial to prevent complications such as aspiration pneumonia. Additionally, a stroke can affect pituitary function, leading to hormonal deficiencies and other health issues. \n\nThe condition is also studied in relation to dietary factors, such as salt consumption, and its association with obesity and cardiovascular health. Overall, ictus is a complex neurological condition that requires careful assessment and management to address the various health challenges it presents."}{"title": "CANCER DE CABEZA Y CUELLO:CANCER DE CABEZA Y CUELLO, or head and neck cancer, is a type of cancer that can significantly impact various functions, including swallowing. This condition is particularly relevant in the context of dysphagia studies, as it can lead to difficulties in swallowing due to the anatomical and functional changes caused by the disease."}{"title": "TOS:Coughing is a reflex action that helps clear the throat and airways, often associated with swallowing difficulties and dysphagia."}{"title": "DIFICULTAD PARA TRAGAR:Difficulty swallowing is a clinical symptom that can indicate various underlying health issues, including dysphagia."}{"title": "BOCA SECA:Dry mouth is a condition that can affect swallowing and is often related to medications taken by patients."}{"title": "RESIDUOS EN LA GARGANTA:Residual food in the throat can lead to swallowing difficulties and is a concern for patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "SIGNOS CL\u00cdNICOS:Clinical signs are indicators that help in diagnosing conditions like dysphagia."}{"title": "PRUEBAS INSTRUMENTALES:Instrumental tests are diagnostic procedures used to assess swallowing function and identify dysphagia."}{"title": "S\u00cdNTOMA IGNORADO:The term refers to conditions like dysphagia that are often overlooked in clinical settings."}{"title": "PREVALENCIA:Prevalencia refers to the commonness of a condition, such as dysphagia, within a specific population. It encompasses the total number of cases of a disease present in a population at a given point in time. This concept is crucial for understanding the extent of health issues within communities and aids in public health planning and resource allocation."}{"title": "MAYOR:"}{"title": "SISTEMA NACIONAL DE SALUD:The Sistema Nacional de Salud (SNS) is the public healthcare system in Spain that provides a wide range of health services to the population. It is responsible for the funding, regulation, and delivery of healthcare services, ensuring health promotion and equity in access to care, as governed by the General Health Law of 1986. The SNS includes various provisions in its portfolio, such as home parenteral nutrition, dietary products, and medical services, and it plays a crucial role in the management and treatment of conditions like diabetes. Additionally, the SNS oversees health services and research, regulating both healthcare delivery and nutrition-related provisions. Overall, the Sistema Nacional de Salud is integral to the health and well-being of the Spanish population, encompassing a comprehensive array of healthcare services and organizations."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE ALZHEIMER:Alzheimer's disease, known as \"enfermedad de Alzheimer\" in Spanish, is the most common form of dementia, primarily affecting the elderly population. It is characterized by a complex pathophysiology and is significantly influenced by age, which is the main risk factor. This neurodegenerative condition leads to severe cognitive decline, including memory loss and behavioral changes. Additionally, it can result in significant swallowing difficulties, impacting up to 80% of patients. Research suggests that Alzheimer's disease may also be influenced by diet and other modifiable risk factors, highlighting the importance of lifestyle choices in its management and prevention."}{"title": "ACCIDENTES CEREBROVASCULARES:Cerebrovascular accidents, commonly known as strokes, can significantly impact patients' health, particularly affecting their ability to swallow. Research indicates that approximately 47% of individuals who experience cerebrovascular accidents may develop dysphagia, a condition characterized by difficulty in swallowing. This impairment can further complicate their nutritional intake, often requiring enteral nutrition support to ensure adequate nourishment and digestion."}{"title": "NEUMON\u00cdA:NEUMON\u00cdA is an infection characterized by the inflammation of the air sacs in one or both lungs, which can fill with fluid or pus, leading to severe respiratory issues. This condition can arise as a complication in patients with various underlying health issues, including muscular diseases such as the s\u00edndrome de Kennedy, where it can significantly affect respiratory function. Additionally, pneumonia is a notable risk for individuals suffering from dysphagia, particularly oropharyngeal dysphagia, as it can lead to aspiration pneumonia. The infection can also induce conditions like SIADH and typically requires a specific duration of treatment. Overall, pneumonia poses a serious health risk, especially for patients with chronic respiratory conditions like EPOC (chronic obstructive pulmonary disease)."}{"title": "PA\u00cdSES DESARROLLADOS:Developed countries are experiencing an increase in the elderly population, which is projected to reach 20% of the population over 65 years old in the near future."}{"title": "DIFICULTADES PARA TRAGAR:\"DIFICULTADES PARA TRAGAR\" refers to difficulties swallowing, a common symptom that affects a significant portion of the population at some point in their lives. These swallowing difficulties can lead to the necessity of modifying one's diet, which may subsequently impact nutritional status."}{"title": "PATOLOG\u00cdA:PATOLOG\u00cdA refers to the study of diseases and their effects on the organism, which is particularly relevant to clinical nutrition. It encompasses various health conditions, including those that can coexist with dysphagia, thereby increasing its prevalence among affected individuals."}{"title": "REINO UNIDO:The United Kingdom, often referred to as \"Reino Unido,\" is a country that has made significant contributions to medical research and public health. It suggests that transplantation should be considered only under specific medical conditions, particularly related to portal hypertension, liver cirrhosis, or fibrosis. The UK has recorded survival rates for patients with short bowel syndrome and has conducted extensive studies on the prevalence of gastrointestinal issues such as constipation and diarrhea.\n\nIn addition to these studies, the United Kingdom has examined the economic costs associated with malnutrition and its impact on public health. It has developed several guidelines for the refeeding of malnourished patients, incorporating recommendations from the Royal College of Psychiatrists and NICE (National Institute for Health and Care Excellence). Research in the UK has also focused on nutritional support and its economic implications, especially concerning malnutrition and home care.\n\nDespite its advancements, the United Kingdom faces limitations in data collection for epidemiological studies, which affects the comprehensiveness of its health data. Notably, significant epidemiological studies on intestinal rhythm have been conducted within the country. Furthermore, the UK has identified a high prevalence of dysphagia among the elderly population and estimates that hereditary fructose intolerance occurs in approximately 1 in 18,000 individuals. The country is also recognized for its clinical guidelines that describe food textures and liquid viscosities, which are essential for patient care. Overall, the United Kingdom is a key player in health research, particularly in areas related to nutrition, gastrointestinal health, and public health policy."}{"title": "FRANCIA:FRANCIA, known as France, is a country that has been highlighted in various studies regarding health issues, particularly dysphagia among older adults, indicating a significant prevalence of this condition within this demographic. Additionally, France is included in the epidemiological study of NED (Nutritional and Eating Disorders), which underscores its relevance in the context of health research. Notably, Francia was one of the pioneering countries to regulate the funding of NED in 1988, demonstrating its proactive approach to addressing nutritional and eating disorders."}{"title": "ALEMANIA:Alemania, also known as Germany, is one of the eight countries that face limitations in data collection for epidemiological studies. Despite these challenges, Germany has reported a lower prevalence of dysphagia among its population, with only 43% of the elderly affected by this condition, which is comparatively lower than in other countries."}{"title": "JAP\u00d3N:Japan is a country located in Asia, known for its unique dietary habits and health-related statistics. Among the elderly population, Japan has reported a prevalence of dysphagia, with figures ranging from 11% to 16% in various studies. To address this issue, Japan has established defined levels of food and liquid textures specifically for patients with dysphagia, ensuring that dietary needs are met.\n\nIn terms of nutrition, Japan is recognized for its high consumption of omega-3 fatty acids, with estimates reaching up to 2 grams per day. This dietary practice is linked to the country's notably low rates of coronary heart disease, attributed to the intake of alpha-linolenic acid (ALA) and other omega-3 fatty acids. Additionally, Japan recommends a daily salt intake of 6 grams, further reflecting its focus on health-conscious dietary guidelines.\n\nDespite these positive health indicators, Japan is also one of the countries with limited data on home nutrition and has been identified as having restrictions in data collection for epidemiological studies. This limitation highlights the need for further research to better understand the nutritional landscape and health challenges faced by its population."}{"title": "PA\u00cdSES BAJOS:The Netherlands has also reported figures related to the prevalence of dysphagia among older adults."}{"title": "NEUMON\u00cdA POR ASPIRACI\u00d3N:NEUMON\u00cdA POR ASPIRACI\u00d3N, also known as aspiration pneumonia, is a lung infection that arises from the inhalation of saliva, food, liquid, or vomit into the lungs. This condition is often linked to dysphagia, which is difficulty swallowing, and can occur as a potential complication in patients receiving nasogastric feeding. The infection is characterized by the introduction of contaminated substances into the respiratory tract, leading to inflammation and infection in the lungs."}{"title": "HAEMOPHILUS INFLUENZAE:Haemophilus influenzae is a bacterium commonly associated with aspiration pneumonia, particularly in patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "STREPTOCOCCUS PNEUMONIAE:Streptococcus pneumoniae is another bacterium linked to aspiration pneumonia, often found in patients with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "KLEBSIELLA PNEUMONIAE:Klebsiella pneumoniae is a bacterium belonging to the Enterobacteriaceae family, known for its association with various infections, particularly catheter-related infections. This pathogen is also capable of causing aspiration pneumonia, especially in vulnerable populations such as the elderly or those with compromised immune systems. Its ability to thrive in hospital settings makes it a significant concern in healthcare-associated infections."}{"title": "ESCHERICHIA COLI:Escherichia coli, commonly known as E. coli, is a type of bacterium that is widely recognized for its role in various infections and gastrointestinal diseases. One notable strain, enterohemorrhagic E. coli, is particularly concerning as it can lead to severe gastrointestinal illness, characterized by diarrhea and abdominal pain. E. coli is also known to cause infections in patients with urinary catheters and other invasive medical devices, making it a significant concern in healthcare settings. Additionally, this bacterium can be implicated in infections related to surgical sites and has been associated with inflammatory bowel disease. In certain cases, E. coli may even contribute to the development of aspiration pneumonia. Overall, E. coli is a versatile bacterium that poses various health risks, particularly in vulnerable populations."}{"title": "PSEUDOMONAS AERUGINOSA:Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a bacterium known for its role in various infections, particularly in individuals with compromised health. It is notably associated with aspiration pneumonia, where it can contribute to respiratory complications. Additionally, Pseudomonas aeruginosa is recognized for its potential to cause infections in patients who have central venous catheters, highlighting its significance in healthcare settings, especially among vulnerable populations."}{"title": "ENFERMEDADES NEURODEGENERATIVAS:\"ENFERMEDADES NEURODEGENERATIVAS\" refers to a group of disorders characterized by the progressive degeneration of the structure and function of the nervous system, which includes conditions such as dementia and Parkinson's disease. These diseases can significantly impact patients' quality of life, often leading to complications such as oropharyngeal dysphagia, which increases the risk of aspiration pneumonia. Specialized nutritional support may be required for individuals suffering from these conditions.\n\nIn Spain, CIBERned is a dedicated research center focused on neurodegenerative diseases, contributing to the understanding and treatment of these disorders. Additionally, neurodegenerative diseases present unique ethical and legal challenges in healthcare decision-making, particularly concerning patients' rights to medical treatment. Overall, the implications of neurodegenerative diseases extend beyond medical concerns, affecting various aspects of patients' lives and the healthcare system."}{"title": "ANTIBIOTICOTERAPIA:Antibiotic therapy, also known as \"ANTIBIOTICOTERAPIA,\" involves the use of antibiotics to treat bacterial infections. This treatment is essential for managing infections that may arise from medical devices such as catheters. However, antibiotic therapy can also have significant effects on the oral flora, potentially increasing the risk of aspiration pneumonia, particularly in patients who experience dysphagia. Thus, while antibiotic therapy plays a critical role in combating bacterial infections, it is important to consider its implications on oral health and the associated risks in vulnerable populations."}{"title": "HIGIENE DENTAL:Dental hygiene is a factor that can affect the risk of aspiration pneumonia, particularly in patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "SENSORIALIDAD LAR\u00cdNGEA:Laryngeal sensitivity is crucial for preventing aspiration; its impairment can lead to increased risk of aspiration pneumonia."}{"title": "REFLEJO TUSIGENO:The cough reflex is an important defense mechanism against aspiration; its dysfunction can lead to aspiration pneumonia."}{"title": "SONDA NASOG\u00c1STRICA:The \"SONDA NASOG\u00c1STRICA\" is a medical device designed for enteral feeding, particularly beneficial for patients suffering from severe dysphagia who are unable to swallow safely. This flexible tube is inserted through the nose and extends into the stomach, allowing for the administration of nutrition and medications. It is primarily utilized in hospital settings, managed by nursing staff, and serves as a temporary solution for hydration and nutritional support.\n\nThe nasogastric tube is indicated for patients with intact gastric function and is used for short to medium-term nutritional support. It facilitates the delivery of hyperosmolar diets and can be employed for continuous or intermittent infusion flows. Additionally, the device is instrumental in assessing the tolerance of infusions and monitoring for significant reflux prior to medical interventions.\n\nWhile the nasogastric tube provides essential nutritional support, its use can also impact a patient's relationship with their environment and self. Furthermore, it may alter the oropharyngeal ecosystem, potentially increasing the risk of aspiration pneumonia. Overall, the \"SONDA NASOG\u00c1STRICA\" is a critical tool in managing the nutritional needs of patients who cannot eat by mouth, ensuring they receive necessary sustenance directly into their stomachs."}{"title": "AUSTRALIA:Australia is a country that plays a significant role in various health-related studies, particularly focusing on malnutrition and dehydration in elderly patients, with 53 hospitals participating in this research. Additionally, Australia has been involved in studying trends in hospital admissions due to anaphylaxis. However, it faces challenges in data collection for epidemiological studies, being one of eight countries noted for such limitations. Furthermore, Australia has conducted studies on the prevalence of malnutrition, contributing valuable comparative data to the field."}{"title": "PREDYCES:PREDYCES is a comprehensive multicenter study conducted in hospitals across Spain, focusing on the nutritional status and prevalence of malnutrition among oncology patients and other hospitalized individuals. The study reveals significant rates of malnutrition both upon admission and discharge, highlighting the critical issue of disease-related malnutrition in this vulnerable population. \n\nPREDYCES specifically assesses the prevalence and impact of malnutrition, including its costs in hospitalized patients, and has analyzed groups such as those with oropharyngeal dysphagia. The research included a sample of 352 patients with dysphagia, demonstrating high rates of malnutrition and emphasizing the detrimental effects of oropharyngeal dysphagia on patients' health and associated hospital costs. Additionally, the study involved the nutritional assessment of diabetic patients across 50 hospitals, further underscoring the widespread issue of malnutrition in various patient groups.\n\nOverall, PREDYCES provides valuable data on the prevalence and consequences of malnutrition in hospitalized patients, aiming to raise awareness and improve nutritional care in clinical settings."}{"title": "MALNUTRITION:Malnutrition is a clinical condition characterized by inadequate intake of nutrients, which can arise from various factors including an unbalanced diet, inability to absorb nutrients, and specific health conditions. It is prevalent among different patient populations, particularly those with liver disease, such as cirrhosis, where it significantly impacts clinical outcomes and can lead to various complications, including protein-energy malnutrition. \n\nIn patients with repeated pancreatitis attacks, nutritional intervention is often required to address malnutrition. Additionally, malnutrition is a common concern in elderly patients, where it can lead to increased fragility and health complications. It is also a significant issue in patients with dysphagia, cancer, and conditions like MELAS syndrome, which have specific nutritional needs. \n\nMalnutrition can be assessed using tools like the Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool (MUST) and the Short Nutritional Assessment Questionnaire (SNAQ). Furthermore, it is recognized as a critical factor affecting the prognosis of patients undergoing intestinal surgery, leading to increased morbidity and prolonged hospital stays. Overall, malnutrition is a significant health issue that requires attention and intervention in various healthcare settings."}{"title": "DEHYDRATION:Dehydration is a condition characterized by a significant loss of body fluids, which can lead to various health complications. It is particularly common among elderly patients, where it can exacerbate malnutrition and contribute to a decline in overall health. Additionally, dehydration can occur in patients with dysphagia, a condition that impairs the ability to swallow liquids effectively, resulting in inadequate fluid intake. This highlights the importance of monitoring fluid consumption in vulnerable populations to prevent dehydration and its associated risks."}{"title": "HOSPITALS:53 hospitals in Australia are involved in the study of malnutrition and dehydration among elderly patients."}{"title": "CAREGIVERS:CAREGIVERS are individuals who provide essential care and support to patients, playing a crucial role in the management of various health conditions, including dementia, disorders of function (DOF), and malnutrition. They face significant challenges due to the complexities of the patients' conditions, requiring them to adapt their caregiving strategies to meet the diverse needs of those they care for."}{"title": "PATIENTS:Patients are individuals undergoing treatment for various health conditions, including dysphagia, cystic fibrosis, and those preparing for bariatric surgery. Specifically, patients with dysphagia often require multidisciplinary approaches for effective rehabilitation, as their condition can lead to increased healthcare costs and longer hospital stays. Additionally, patients undergoing bariatric surgery may face complications such as dumping syndrome and changes in bone density. Furthermore, patients with cystic fibrosis necessitate dietary management and supplementation to enhance their health outcomes. Overall, the care and management of these patients involve addressing complex medical needs and potential complications associated with their conditions."}{"title": "NHDS:The National Hospital Discharge Survey (NHDS) is a study that evaluates hospital discharge data to assess patient outcomes and healthcare utilization."}{"title": "AHRQ:The Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality (AHRQ) is involved in evaluating healthcare costs and utilization, including studies on dysphagia."}{"title": "UNITED STATES:The United States is a country located in North America, recognized for its significant influence on global politics and economics. It has a high prevalence of obesity, with approximately 34% of its population affected. Additionally, the United States is the site where studies on the prevalence of dysphagia and its impact on hospital stays and associated costs were conducted."}{"title": "DENMARK:Denmark is one of the five northern European countries that contributed to the establishment of the ERAS group. Additionally, it is the country where a study was conducted to evaluate the costs associated with dysphagia in geriatric patients."}{"title": "HOSPITALIZACI\u00d3N:Hospitalizaci\u00f3n refers to the process of being admitted to a hospital for medical care, which may be necessary for various conditions, including head and neck cancers, acute pancreatitis, severe diarrhea, and complications related to liver disease. During hospitalization, patients often face challenges such as dysphagia, which can lead to longer hospital stays compared to those without such issues. Nutritional support is critical during this period, especially for patients at risk of malnutrition, including frail elderly individuals who may experience hospitalization due to stress factors and their frailty. \n\nIn cases of severe malnutrition, hospitalization involves close monitoring and treatment to address related complications. Additionally, hospitalization can be a stressful event, particularly for elderly patients, potentially exacerbating their fragility. It is also relevant in the context of patients undergoing specific treatment protocols, such as the ketogenic diet, where medical supervision is essential. Furthermore, hospitalization may be necessary for psychiatric treatment, especially in cases involving eating disorders. Overall, the hospitalization process is a crucial aspect of medical care that addresses both physical and nutritional needs of patients across various health conditions."}{"title": "COSTES ASOCIADOS:Associated costs refer to the financial burden incurred due to longer hospital stays and additional care required for patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "REINGRESOS:Readmissions refer to the instances when patients return to the hospital after discharge, which are more frequent for those with dysphagia."}{"title": "PACIENTES HOSPITALIZADOS:\"PACIENTES HOSPITALIZADOS\" refers to individuals who are receiving treatment in a hospital setting. This group is particularly vulnerable to various health complications, including a notable percentage diagnosed with dysphagia, which is a condition that affects swallowing. Additionally, hospitalized patients are at a high risk of malnutrition, a prevalent issue that can further complicate their overall health status."}{"title": "PACIENTES GERI\u00c1TRICOS:Geriatric patients, referred to as \"PACIENTES GERI\u00c1TRICOS,\" are a specific group of older adults who face unique health challenges, particularly related to disease-related malnutrition, as emphasized in the PREDYCES study. This demographic is more susceptible to dysphagia, a condition that complicates their ability to eat and drink, leading to increased healthcare costs. Additionally, geriatric patients often require specialized nutritional care due to their health conditions and specific dietary needs. Overall, this group necessitates careful attention to their nutritional and healthcare requirements to improve their quality of life."}{"title": "PNEUMONIA POR ASPIRACI\u00d3N:"}{"title": "SARCOMA:Sarcoma is a type of malignant tumor that can affect the selar region and originates in connective tissues. It is important to note that sarcoma is distinct from sarcopenia, which is a condition that can accompany oropharyngeal dysphagia, particularly in older adults, impacting their health and quality of life. While both terms relate to health issues, sarcoma specifically refers to a cancerous growth, whereas sarcopenia pertains to muscle loss and its associated complications."}{"title": "LANCASTER J.:Lancaster J. is an author who has contributed to the understanding of dysphagia, including its nature, assessment, and management."}{"title": "CHICHERO J.:Chichero J. is an author who has researched the definition, prevalence, and burden of oropharyngeal dysphagia, particularly among older adults."}{"title": "VELASCO MM.:Velasco MM. is an author who has focused on the nutritional approach to oropharyngeal dysphagia, including diagnosis and treatment."}{"title": "GONZALEZ R.:Gonzalez R. is an author who has studied dysphagia in neurological patients."}{"title": "MORBIMORTALITY:Morbimortality refers to the combined incidence of morbidity and mortality, encompassing various health risks associated with different conditions. It is particularly relevant in the context of preterm newborns, where the risks of disease and death are heightened. Additionally, morbimortality is significant in relation to oropharyngeal dysphagia, which can lead to serious complications such as aspiration pneumonia and malnutrition. Furthermore, it also pertains to the incidence of disease and death linked to health conditions, especially concerning nutritional deficiencies in chronic patients. Overall, morbimortality serves as a critical measure of health outcomes across diverse populations and medical conditions."}{"title": "QUALITY OF LIFE:Quality of life for patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia is significantly affected due to difficulties in swallowing and associated health issues."}{"title": "MULTIDISCIPLINARY APPROACH:The \"MULTIDISCIPLINARY APPROACH\" refers to a collaborative strategy in healthcare that involves various professionals working together to deliver comprehensive care. This approach is particularly important in the treatment of conditions such as oropharyngeal dysphagia and in the field of ELA (English Language Arts) treatment. By integrating the expertise of different healthcare providers, a multidisciplinary approach ensures effective diagnosis and treatment, ultimately enhancing patient outcomes."}{"title": "PREVENTIVE MEASURES:Preventive measures are essential to improve the clinical situation and quality of life for patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia."}{"title": "HOSPITAL COSTS:"}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA EN MEDICINA:\"NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA EN MEDICINA\" is a medical journal that focuses on clinical approaches to various health issues, including dysphagia management. In 2007, it published an article specifically addressing the nutritional approach to oropharyngeal dysphagia, highlighting its commitment to providing valuable insights and research in the field of clinical nutrition."}{"title": "REV HOSP CLIN UNIV CHILE:A medical journal that published research on dysphagia in neurological patients in 2009"}{"title": "CLIN NEUROPHYSIOL:A journal that published a study on the neurophysiology of swallowing in 2003"}{"title": "TEXAS:A state in the United States where the manual for videofluoroscopic study of swallowing was published"}{"title": "J NEUROL NEUROSURG PSYCHIATRY:The entity \"J NEUROL NEUROSURG PSYCHIATRY,\" also known as The Journal of Neurology, Neurosurgery, and Psychiatry, is a scholarly journal that focuses on publishing research related to the fields of neurology and psychiatry. Notably, in 2003, the journal published an article addressing the neurology of swallowing and oral feeding disorders. Additionally, it features studies that explore the relationship between diet and cognitive health, contributing to the broader understanding of how neurological and psychiatric conditions can be influenced by dietary factors."}{"title": "GASTROENTEROLOGY:Gastroenterology is a specialized branch of medicine that focuses on the digestive system and its disorders. This field encompasses the diagnosis and treatment of various conditions affecting the digestive tract, including but not limited to pancreatitis, Crohn's disease, and liver diseases. Gastroenterology also involves nutritional management, particularly in cases requiring parenteral nutrition.\n\nIn addition to its clinical aspects, Gastroenterology is represented by a leading peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes significant research and guidelines related to digestive health. This journal covers a wide range of topics, including studies on swallowing, dysphagia, dietary factors, cancer risk, and complications associated with liver cirrhosis. Notably, the journal published a study in 1997 that examined the coordination of deglutitive glottal function and pharyngeal bolus transit.\n\nOverall, Gastroenterology plays a crucial role in advancing the understanding and treatment of digestive system disorders, contributing to both clinical practice and academic research in the field."}{"title": "GI MOTILITY:An online publication that discussed the coordination of respiration and swallowing in 2006"}{"title": "DYSPHAGIA:Dysphagia is a medical condition characterized by difficulty in swallowing, which can significantly impact a patient's quality of life and nutritional intake. It is commonly observed in patients with various conditions, including amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, dementia, and esophageal cancer. Dysphagia can lead to serious complications such as malnutrition and dehydration, necessitating multidisciplinary solutions for effective management. The condition is often studied in relation to various therapies and interventions, and it is the focus of numerous dietary guidelines and research efforts. Additionally, dysphagia can occur after a stroke, affecting patient outcomes and requiring thorough assessment and management. In 2010, a journal published an article discussing supranuclear control of swallowing, highlighting the ongoing research and interest in understanding and addressing this swallowing impairment."}{"title": "CLIN INTERV IN AGING:A journal that published a review on oropharyngeal dysphagia in older persons in 2016"}{"title": "PLOS ONE:PLOS ONE is a multidisciplinary peer-reviewed open-access journal that publishes research across all areas of science and medicine. Established to facilitate the dissemination of scientific knowledge, PLOS ONE covers a wide range of topics, including nutrition, cancer, and dietary factors. The journal is known for its commitment to open access, allowing researchers and the public to access its articles freely.\n\nIn 2011, PLOS ONE published a significant study on the cortical processing of swallowing in patients with Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis (ALS), highlighting its role in advancing medical research. Additionally, the journal has featured systematic reviews and meta-analyses, such as those examining the impact of fruit and vegetable consumption on anthropometric changes and the relationship between red and processed meat intake and gastric cancer risk.\n\nOverall, PLOS ONE serves as a vital platform for the publication of diverse scientific research, contributing to the advancement of knowledge across various fields."}{"title": "EDITORIAL GLOSA:Editorial Glosa is a publishing house based in Barcelona that specializes in the publication of medical guides. Notably, it published a comprehensive guide on the diagnosis and nutritional treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia, which addresses both the clinical and rehabilitative aspects of this condition."}{"title": "CIR ESP:A journal that published an article on the diagnosis and treatment of functional oropharyngeal dysphagia in 2007"}{"title": "ARREOLA V:Arreola V is a notable contributor to the field of swallowing disorders, particularly in the context of oropharyngeal dysphagia. He played a significant role as one of the authors of a comprehensive guide focused on the diagnosis and nutritional treatment of this condition. Additionally, Arreola V co-authored an article published in 2007 in the journal Nutrici\u00f3n Cl\u00ednica en Medicina, which specifically addressed the nutritional approach to managing oropharyngeal dysphagia. His research and contributions are instrumental in advancing understanding and treatment strategies for swallowing disorders."}{"title": "CLAVE P:Clave P is a prominent researcher and author recognized for his significant contributions to the field of dysphagia, particularly in the area of swallowing therapies. He played a key role in developing the diagnostic and nutritional treatment guidelines for oropharyngeal dysphagia. Additionally, Clav\u00e9 P co-authored an article on the nutritional approach to oropharyngeal dysphagia, which was published in the journal Nutrici\u00f3n Cl\u00ednica en Medicina in 2007. His work has been instrumental in advancing the understanding and management of dysphagia."}{"title": "PUIGGR\u00d3S C:PUIGGR\u00d3S C is recognized as a co-author of an article focused on the nutritional approach to oropharyngeal dysphagia, which was published in the journal Nutrici\u00f3n Cl\u00ednica en Medicina in 2007. Additionally, Puiggr\u00f3s C contributes to the Spanish registry of home-based enteral nutrition and is actively involved in related research efforts."}{"title": "GONZALEZ R:Author of the article on dysphagia in neurological patients published in Rev Hosp Clin Univ Chile in 2009"}{"title": "BEVILCQUA JA:Co-author of the article on dysphagia in neurological patients published in Rev Hosp Clin Univ Chile in 2009"}{"title": "ETERKIN C:Author of the study on neurophysiology of swallowing published in Clin Neurophysiol in 2003"}{"title": "AYDOGDU I:Co-author of the study on neurophysiology of swallowing published in Clin Neurophysiol in 2003"}{"title": "HUGHES T:Author of the article on neurology of swallowing and oral feeding disorders published in J Neurol Neurosurg Psychiatry in 2003"}{"title": "DUA KS:Co-author of the study on coordination of deglutitive glottal function published in Gastroenterology in 1997"}{"title": "REN J:Co-author of the study on coordination of deglutitive glottal function published in Gastroenterology in 1997"}{"title": "BARDAN E:Co-author of the study on coordination of deglutitive glottal function published in Gastroenterology in 1997"}{"title": "XIE P:Co-author of the study on coordination of deglutitive glottal function published in Gastroenterology in 1997"}{"title": "SHAKER R:SHAKER R is a notable contributor to the field of dysphagia research, having co-authored a review on oropharyngeal dysphagia in older persons, which was published in the journal Clinical Interventions in Aging in 2016. Additionally, SHAKE R co-authored a study focused on the coordination of deglutitive glottal function, published in Gastroenterology in 1997. These contributions highlight SHAKE R's expertise and involvement in advancing the understanding of swallowing disorders and their implications in different populations."}{"title": "MARTIN-HARRIS B:Author of the article on coordination of respiration and swallowing published in GI Motility in 2006"}{"title": "LEOPOLD NA:Co-author of the article on supranuclear control of swallowing published in Dysphagia in 2010"}{"title": "DANIELS SK:Co-author of the article on supranuclear control of swallowing published in Dysphagia in 2010"}{"title": "WIRTH R:WIRTH R is a co-author of a review on oropharyngeal dysphagia in older persons, which was published in the journal Clinical Interventions in Aging in 2016. In this capacity, Wirth R contributed to the examination of oropharyngeal dysphagia and the various interventions related to this condition in the elderly population."}{"title": "DZIEWAS R:DZIEWAS R is a co-author of a review on oropharyngeal dysphagia in older persons, which was published in the journal Clinical Interventions in Aging in 2016. Additionally, Dziewas R contributed to the review of dysphagia interventions specifically aimed at older individuals, highlighting their expertise in this area of research."}{"title": "BECK AM:Beck AM is an author recognized for their contributions to the field of dysphagia interventions. They have co-authored a review focused on oropharyngeal dysphagia in older individuals, which was published in the journal Clinical Interventions in Aging in 2016. Additionally, Beck AM has collaborated on research concerning texture modified foods specifically designed for individuals with dysphagia, further highlighting their involvement in improving dietary options for this population."}{"title": "CLAV\u00c9 P:Clav\u00e9 P is an author recognized for their contributions to the field of dysphagia interventions. They co-authored a review specifically focused on oropharyngeal dysphagia in older individuals, which was published in the journal Clinical Interventions in Aging in 2016."}{"title": "HAMDY S:Hamdy S is a co-author of a review on oropharyngeal dysphagia in older persons, which was published in the journal Clinical Interventions in Aging in 2016. In addition to this, Hamdy S contributed to the review of dysphagia interventions, highlighting their involvement in the research and literature surrounding this important health issue."}{"title": "HEPPNER HJ:Heppner HJ is a notable author who co-authored a review on oropharyngeal dysphagia in older persons, which was published in the journal Clinical Interventions in Aging in 2016. His contributions to the review focused on dysphagia interventions, highlighting his involvement in addressing this important health issue."}{"title": "LANGMORE S:Co-author of the review on oropharyngeal dysphagia in older persons published in Clin Interv in Aging in 2016"}{"title": "LEISCHKER AH:Co-author of the review on oropharyngeal dysphagia in older persons published in Clin Interv in Aging in 2016"}{"title": "MARTINO R:MARTINO R is a notable figure in the field of dysphagia research, recognized for his contributions to the understanding and assessment of swallowing disorders in older adults. He co-authored a review on oropharyngeal dysphagia in older persons, which was published in the journal Clinical Interventions in Aging in 2016. Additionally, Martino R is credited with the development and validation of the Toronto Bedside Swallowing Screening Test (TOR-BSST), a tool specifically designed for evaluating swallowing function in patients who have experienced a stroke. His work has significantly advanced the knowledge and clinical practices related to swallowing difficulties in vulnerable populations."}{"title": "PLUSCHINSKI P:Co-author of the review on oropharyngeal dysphagia in older persons published in Clin Interv in Aging in 2016"}{"title": "R\u00d6SLER A:Co-author of the review on oropharyngeal dysphagia in older persons published in Clin Interv in Aging in 2016"}{"title": "WARNECKE T:Warnecke T is a notable author recognized for contributions to the field of dysphagia, particularly in older adults and individuals with Parkinson's Disease. In 2016, Warnecke T co-authored a review on oropharyngeal dysphagia in older persons, which was published in the journal Clinical Interventions in Aging. This work highlights the complexities and challenges associated with swallowing difficulties in the aging population. Additionally, Warnecke T has also focused on dysphagia specifically related to Parkinson's Disease, further emphasizing the importance of understanding and addressing swallowing disorders in various patient groups."}{"title": "SIEBER CC:Co-author of the review on oropharyngeal dysphagia in older persons published in Clin Interv in Aging in 2016"}{"title": "VOLKERT D:VOLKERT D is a prominent researcher known for his contributions to the field of geriatric nutrition. He co-authored a review on oropharyngeal dysphagia in older persons, which was published in the journal Clinical Interventions in Aging in 2016. In addition to this, Volkert D has published guidelines focused on nutritional interventions specifically designed for older adults. His research also encompasses the study of the relationship between nutrition and frailty, highlighting the importance of dietary considerations in the health and well-being of the elderly population."}{"title": "TEISMANN I:Co-author of the study on cortical processing of swallowing in ALS patients published in PLOS One in 2011"}{"title": "SUNTRUP S:Co-author of the study on cortical processing of swallowing in ALS patients published in PLOS One in 2011"}{"title": "CLAV\u00c9 CIVIT P:Co-author of the guide on diagnosis and nutritional treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia published in Barcelona"}{"title": "GARC\u00cdA PERIS P:Garc\u00eda Peris P is a notable figure in the field of clinical nutrition, recognized for several significant contributions. They co-authored a guide on the diagnosis and nutritional treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia, which was published in Barcelona. Additionally, Garc\u00eda Peris P is referenced in the bibliography concerning hospital malnutrition coding, highlighting their involvement in addressing malnutrition in healthcare settings. Their research also extends to dietary fiber and its implications in clinical nutrition, showcasing their commitment to advancing knowledge in this area. Furthermore, Garc\u00eda Peris P has contributed to the development of nutritional recommendations for individuals with inflammatory bowel disease, further emphasizing their expertise and influence in the field of nutrition."}{"title": "MALDHI H:Author of the article on dysphagia warning signs and management published in Br J Nurs in 2016"}{"title": "JANSSON-KNODELL CI:Co-author of the review on making dysphagia easier to swallow published in Mayo Clin Proc in 2017"}{"title": "CODIPILLY CH:Co-author of the review on making dysphagia easier to swallow published in Mayo Clin Proc in 2017"}{"title": "LEGGETT CL:Co-author of the review on making dysphagia easier to swallow published in Mayo Clin Proc in 2017"}{"title": "VELASCO MM:"}{"title": "ROSA ANA ASHBAUGH ENGU\u00cdDANOS:Rosa Ana Ashbaugh Engu\u00eddanos is a professional dedicated to the study and promotion of oral hygiene and its significance in health care. In addition to her work in oral hygiene, she is also a researcher focused on oropharyngeal dysphagia, specifically exploring its screening methods. Through her dual involvement in these areas, she contributes to enhancing understanding and practices related to oral health and swallowing disorders."}{"title": "ESPEN GUIDELINES 2017:The ESPEN Guidelines 2017 provide recommendations for the management and treatment of dysphagia."}{"title": "BARNES-JEWISH HOSPITAL STROKE DYSPHAGIA SCREEN:The Barnes-Jewish Hospital Stroke Dysphagia Screen is a specific method for assessing dysphagia in stroke patients."}{"title": "SWALLOW QUESTIONNAIRE:The Swallow Questionnaire is a tool utilized to assess swallowing difficulties in patients. It is specifically designed to measure the quality of life and subjective symptoms experienced by individuals with dysphagia, providing valuable insights into their condition and helping to guide treatment decisions."}{"title": "EATING ASSESSMENT TOOL-10:The Eating Assessment Tool-10 is a screening tool specifically designed to assess dysphagia in patients. It functions as a self-evaluation scale that enables individuals to evaluate their own clinical symptoms related to dysphagia. This tool is instrumental in identifying difficulties in swallowing, thereby facilitating appropriate clinical interventions."}{"title": "PREDYCES STUDY:The PREDyCES Study is a comprehensive research initiative that investigates the prevalence and costs associated with malnutrition in hospitalized patients, specifically focusing on those with diabetes mellitus and dysphagia. This study aims to analyze the extent of hospital malnutrition among these patient groups, highlighting the significant health and economic implications of this condition in a hospital setting. Through its multifaceted approach, the PREDyCES Study seeks to provide valuable insights into the challenges posed by malnutrition in healthcare, ultimately contributing to improved patient care and resource allocation."}{"title": "DYSFAGIA:Dysfagia, also known as dysphagia, is a medical condition characterized by difficulty in swallowing. This condition can significantly impact patients' health and quality of life, leading to serious complications such as aspiration, malnutrition, and dehydration, particularly in patients with conditions like ELA (Early Life Autism) and those who have suffered strokes. Various organizations provide resources related to dysphagia, and it can be assessed using a range of screening methods, scales, and tools designed to improve nutritional recommendations and enhance patient independence. Additionally, technological interventions, including virtual reality, have been explored as potential solutions to address the challenges associated with dysphagia."}{"title": "INSTITUTO NACIONAL DE ESTAD\u00cdSTICA:"}{"title": "ENFERMERAS:Enfermeras, or nurses, are healthcare professionals who play a crucial role in the assessment and care of patients, particularly in the area of enteral nutrition. They are trained to utilize the SSA (Swallowing Screening Assessment) for detecting dysphagia, demonstrating specific sensitivity and specificity rates in its application. Additionally, nurses are fundamental in identifying signs of swallowing disorders and providing necessary care to patients who are at risk of dysphagia. Their expertise is essential in ensuring the well-being of patients requiring specialized nutritional support and monitoring for swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "S\u00cdNTOMAS DE LA DOF:Symptoms of dysphagia orofar\u00edngea include difficulty swallowing, nasal regurgitation, and weight loss, among others."}{"title": "PROGRAMAS DE DETECCI\u00d3N:Programs aimed at early detection, diagnosis, and treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia to reduce morbidity and mortality."}{"title": "HERRAMIENTAS VALIDADAS:Validated tools that assist in the early detection of oropharyngeal dysphagia, applicable to all patients at risk."}{"title": "S\u00cdNTOMAS MANIFIESTOS:Manifest symptoms of dysphagia include difficulty swallowing, nasal regurgitation, and coughing during food intake."}{"title": "S\u00cdNTOMAS SILENTES:Silent symptoms of dysphagia may include changes in eating habits and respiratory infections."}{"title": "CALIDAD DE VIDA:\"Calidad de vida\" refers to the general well-being and life satisfaction of individuals and societies, encompassing various factors that can influence this state. It is particularly relevant in the context of health conditions and interventions, such as in patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (EPOC), chronic gastrointestinal symptoms, and neurological diseases. The quality of life can be negatively affected by these health issues, but it can also be improved through adequate nutritional treatment and medical care.\n\nIn healthcare, quality of life is often measured through cost-utility analyses and questionnaires, which assess how various factors, including nutrition and underlying health conditions, impact an individual's overall well-being. For instance, patients suffering from dysphagia experience significant challenges that affect their social and emotional well-being, but early intervention and treatment can lead to improvements in their quality of life.\n\nMoreover, the impact of cancer and its treatment on quality of life underscores the importance of nutritional support, as it can significantly enhance the overall well-being of patients. Thus, \"calidad de vida\" encompasses a holistic view of health, emphasizing the interplay between medical treatments, caregiving responsibilities, and the nutritional status of individuals, ultimately highlighting the importance of tailored interventions to improve life satisfaction and well-being."}{"title": "TRASTORNOS DE LA DEGLUCI\u00d3N:"}{"title": "DR. P. CLAV\u00c9 CIVIT:Dr. P. Clav\u00e9 Civit is a medical professional who designed the clinical exploration method for assessing swallowing disorders, known as MECV-V or V-VST."}{"title": "M\u00c9TODO DE EXPLORACI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA VOLUMEN-VISCOSIDAD:The M\u00e9todo de Exploraci\u00f3n Cl\u00ednica Volumen-Viscosidad (MECV-V) is a non-invasive clinical assessment method specifically designed to evaluate dysphagia, which is a condition characterized by difficulty in swallowing. This method involves administering food at varying volumes and viscosities to assess the safety and efficacy of swallowing. By utilizing different bolus characteristics, the MECV-V aims to provide a comprehensive evaluation of an individual's swallowing capabilities, ensuring a thorough understanding of their condition."}{"title": "ACIDENTE CEREBROVASCULAR AGUDO:Acute cerebrovascular accident (ACVA) refers to a medical emergency that can lead to swallowing difficulties, necessitating specific screening methods for dysphagia."}{"title": "BOLUS:BOLUS refers to a mass of substance, typically food or liquid, that is swallowed. It plays a crucial role in the assessment of swallowing disorders, as it is the material that is evaluated during such assessments. Specifically, the bolus is the mass of food that is prepared in the oral cavity for swallowing, making it an essential component in understanding and diagnosing swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "PULSOX\u00cdMETRO:A pulse oximeter is a medical device used to monitor the oxygen saturation of a patient's blood, often used during swallowing assessments to detect silent aspirations."}{"title": "MOVILIDAD DE LA MAND\u00cdBULA:Jaw mobility involves the movement of the jaw in various directions, which is crucial for effective chewing and swallowing."}{"title": "SENSIBILIDAD OROFAR\u00cdNGEA:Oropharyngeal sensitivity refers to the ability to feel sensations in the oral and pharyngeal areas, which is important for triggering the swallowing reflex."}{"title": "CAPACIDAD DE LIMPIEZA DE LOS SURCOS GINGIVOLABIALES:The ability to clean the gingivolabial sulcus is important for maintaining oral hygiene and preventing swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "CAPACIDAD DE REALIZAR EL TIPPEER:The ability to perform the Tippeer involves specific tongue movements that are important for swallowing."}{"title": "CALIDAD VOCAL:Vocal quality refers to the characteristics of a person's voice, which can indicate issues related to swallowing and airway protection."}{"title": "RETARDO DEL DISPARO DEGLUTORIO:Swallowing delay refers to the time taken for the swallowing reflex to initiate after food or liquid is presented, which is critical in assessing swallowing function."}{"title": "SIGNOS DE SEGURIDAD:Safety signs are indicators observed during swallowing assessments that help determine if the swallowing process is safe."}{"title": "SIGNOS DE EFICACIA DE LA DEGLUCI\u00d3N:Efficacy signs refer to the indicators that show how effectively a person can swallow without residue or aspiration."}{"title": "MASTICACI\u00d3N:"}{"title": "MECV-V:MECV-V is a clinical exploration method designed to assess the volume-viscosity needs of patients with dysphagia, particularly those who have experienced a stroke. This bedside exploration method involves a structured protocol that outlines a step-by-step process for testing swallowing with various viscosities and volumes. The MECV-V serves as a valuable tool for evaluating swallowing safety and efficiency, helping to diagnose the specific swallowing difficulties faced by patients suspected of having oropharyngeal dysphagia. Overall, MECV-V is instrumental in the clinical follow-up and management of dysphagia in affected individuals."}{"title": "DAVID G SMITHARD:David G Smithard is a professional who co-designed the Standardized Bedside Swallowing Assessment (SSA) for detecting dysphagia."}{"title": "RASEMARY WYATT:Rasemary Wyatt is a professional who co-designed the Standardized Bedside Swallowing Assessment (SSA) for detecting dysphagia."}{"title": "SSA:The SSA, or Standardized Bedside Swallowing Assessment, is a clinical tool utilized to evaluate swallowing function and identify dysphagia. It is designed to provide scientific rigor in the detection of dysphagia, making it a reliable assessment method. The SSA is particularly beneficial for non-expert professionals, enabling them to effectively detect oropharyngeal dysphagia."}{"title": "FEES:FEES, or Fiberoptic Endoscopic Evaluation of Swallowing, is an instrumental test designed to study and assess swallowing disorders. This procedure, also referred to as fibroendoscopy of swallowing, is utilized to evaluate the physiology of swallowing in patients experiencing dysphagia. Through this evaluation, healthcare professionals can gain insights into the mechanics of swallowing and identify any abnormalities or issues that may be present."}{"title": "VIDEOFLOUROSCOPIA:VIDEOFLOUROSCOPIA is a diagnostic imaging technique that plays a crucial role in evaluating swallowing function, particularly in patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia. This method allows for the observation of the swallowing process through real-time X-ray imaging, providing both lateral and anteroposterior projections. It is considered the gold standard for diagnosing dysphagia, as it comprehensively studies the three phases of swallowing. During the procedure, barium is used to enhance visualization, enabling healthcare professionals to assess the pharyngeal phase of swallowing effectively. Videofluoroscopy is particularly recommended when other assessment methods, such as Fiberoptic Endoscopic Evaluation of Swallowing (FEES), are not feasible. Overall, videofluoroscopy is an essential tool in the diagnosis and management of swallowing disorders."}{"title": "AGUDA:Aguda refers to acute neurological conditions in patients that may affect swallowing."}{"title": "OXIMETR\u00cdA:Oximetr\u00eda is a method utilized to evaluate swallowing safety, often in conjunction with water tests. It serves as a screening tool for dysphagia, which involves monitoring symptoms that may arise after a patient is given liquids. This approach helps in assessing the patient's ability to swallow safely and effectively."}{"title": "AGUA:AGUA refers to water, an essential fluid required for hydration and various bodily functions. It plays a critical role in cooking and baking, including the preparation of desserts. In healthcare settings, AGUA is vital for the hydration needs of hospitalized patients, with daily requirements typically ranging from 30 to 40 mL/kg. It is also used to dilute medications for proper delivery through enteral feeding tubes and is a key component in clinical nutrition products, affecting the hydration and stability of ingredients.\n\nThe recommended daily intake of AGUA varies based on body weight, age, and activity level, and it is crucial for maintaining hydration, especially during physical exercise, where it aids in cooling, nutrient delivery, and waste elimination. In patients undergoing hematopoietic transplants, monitoring the balance of AGUA is essential for their dietary needs. Additionally, AGUA is important for maintaining hydration and electrolyte balance in enteral nutrition.\n\nAGUA is a gluten-free beverage and is often assessed in nutritional evaluations for its critical role in overall health. It is also used for cleaning feeding tubes and ensuring patient oral hygiene. While AGUA can contain sodium, particularly in mineral waters, it is generally recommended that its consumption does not correlate with weight variations. Overall, AGUA is a vital nutrient necessary for life, contributing significantly to hydration and health, particularly in children."}{"title": "DEPIPPO KL:DePippo KL is a researcher who developed and validated the oximetry test for dysphagia screening."}{"title": "GUGGING SWALLOWING SCREEN:The Gugging Swallowing Screen (GUSS) is a clinical tool specifically designed to assess swallowing ability and the severity of dysphagia. It was developed in collaboration with the University of Danube Krems in Austria, highlighting its academic foundation and clinical relevance."}{"title": "LANDESKLINIKUM DONAUREGION GUGGING:Landesklinikum Donauregion Gugging is a medical institution in Austria where the GUSS was designed."}{"title": "UNIVERSITY OF DANUBE KREMS:The University of Danube Krems is an academic institution in Austria that collaborated in the development of the GUSS."}{"title": "AQUA BI:Aqua bi is a liquid solution utilized in clinical assessments to evaluate swallowing ability, particularly in the context of dysphagia management. It is specifically employed in the direct swallowing test of the Gugging Swallowing Screen (GUSS), where it is used in conjunction with food thickeners to assess an individual's swallowing capabilities."}{"title": "FOOD THICKENER:Food thickener is a substance used to modify the consistency of liquids for patients with dysphagia during swallowing assessments."}{"title": "DIRECT SWALLOWING TEST:The Direct Swallowing Test is a part of the GUSS that evaluates a patient's ability to swallow different consistencies of food and liquids."}{"title": "INDIRECT SWALLOWING TEST:The Indirect Swallowing Test is a preliminary assessment in the GUSS that evaluates a patient's alertness and ability to manage saliva."}{"title": "PATIENT:The term \"PATIENT\" encompasses a diverse group of individuals receiving medical care, each with unique health conditions and treatment needs. Among them is a 29-year-old woman diagnosed with MELAS, who experiences multiple neurological and gastrointestinal symptoms and requires chronic treatment. Additionally, there is a 76-year-old male patient suffering from type 2 diabetes and moderate to severe malnutrition, necessitating specialized nutritional support and monitoring.\n\nPatients, in general, may include those undergoing nutritional assessments and treatments, particularly individuals at risk of malnutrition or those managing various health conditions such as diabetes. This includes individuals who may require dietary management, lifestyle changes, and specific nutritional plans tailored to their health needs. For instance, patients with diabetes often need individualized nutrition strategies to effectively manage their condition.\n\nFurthermore, the patient population also includes individuals undergoing evaluations for swallowing disorders, obesity, and related health issues, as well as those requiring nutritional support due to oncological conditions, such as a neuroendocrine tumor of the pancreas. Some patients may be preparing for or recovering from bariatric surgery, which involves adhering to specific dietary recommendations.\n\nOverall, the term \"PATIENT\" refers to individuals receiving medical care across a spectrum of health challenges, highlighting the importance of tailored nutritional assessment and support in their treatment plans."}{"title": "SPEECH AND LANGUAGE THERAPIST:A Speech and Language Therapist (SLT) is a professional who assesses and treats communication and swallowing disorders."}{"title": "TORONTO BEDSIDE SWALLOWING SCREENING TEST:The Toronto Bedside Swallowing Screening Test (TOR-BSST) is a validated tool for early detection of oropharyngeal dysphagia."}{"title": "VIDEOFLOUROSCOPIC EVALUATION OF SWALLOWING:Videofluoroscopic Evaluation of Swallowing (VFES) is a diagnostic procedure that uses X-ray technology to assess swallowing function."}{"title": "FIBEROPTIC ENDOSCOPIC EVALUATION OF SWALLOWING:Fiberoptic Endoscopic Evaluation of Swallowing (FEES) is an instrumental assessment method recommended for evaluating swallowing function in patients with dysphagia. This procedure utilizes an endoscope to visualize the swallowing process, allowing for a detailed assessment of any swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "ACVA:ACVA refers to Accidente Cerebrovascular, the Spanish term for stroke, which is medically known as an acute cerebrovascular accident. This condition is a medical emergency that affects blood flow to the brain and can result in significant health complications. One of the potential consequences of an ACVA is dysphagia, or swallowing difficulties, which necessitates careful management to address these challenges. Overall, ACVA encompasses the critical nature of strokes and their impact on patients' health, particularly regarding swallowing functions."}{"title": "DYSPHAGIA DIET:Dysphagia diet refers to dietary modifications made for individuals with swallowing difficulties, including pureed and soft foods."}{"title": "BARNES-JEWISH HOSPITAL:Barnes-Jewish Hospital is a medical facility located in St. Louis, Missouri, known for its stroke care and speech pathology services."}{"title": "STROKE:Stroke is a medical condition characterized by the interruption of blood supply to the brain, which can result in long-term disabilities. It is often included as a background condition in frailty assessments. Dietary factors, such as potassium intake and the consumption of fruits and vegetables, can influence the risk of stroke. Additionally, specialized assessments, such as the BJH Stroke Dysphagia Screen, are utilized to evaluate individuals who have experienced a stroke."}{"title": "BJH STROKE DYSPHAGIA SCREEN:The BJH Stroke Dysphagia Screen is a method developed by Barnes-Jewish Hospital for early detection of dysphagia in stroke patients."}{"title": "SPEECH PATHOLOGY SERVICES:Speech Pathology Services at Barnes-Jewish Hospital provide assessments and interventions for patients with swallowing disorders."}{"title": "GLASGOW COMA SCALE:The Glasgow Coma Scale is a neurological scale used to assess a patient's level of consciousness, particularly in stroke patients."}{"title": "MODIFIED MANN ASSESSMENT OF SWALLOWING:The Modified Mann Assessment of Swallowing is a screening tool used to identify patients with dysphagia and refer them for further evaluation."}{"title": "ST. LOUIS:St. Louis is a city in Missouri, home to Barnes-Jewish Hospital and known for its medical facilities."}{"title": "PATIENCE:The patient is the individual undergoing assessment for swallowing capabilities and reactions to stimuli."}{"title": "SUITER:Suiter is an author referenced in the document, known for research on dysphagia and swallowing assessments."}{"title": "LEDER:Leder is an author referenced in the document, known for contributions to the study of dysphagia."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF CLINICAL NURSING:The Journal of Clinical Nursing is a publication where Perry's work on swallowing assessments was published."}{"title": "DYSHPHAGIA:Dysphagia refers to difficulty in swallowing, which is the primary focus of the assessments described in the document."}{"title": "ARCHIVES OF NEUROLOGY:The \"Archives of Neurology\" is a scholarly publication that focuses on studies related to various neurological conditions, including dementia and cognitive decline. Additionally, it serves as a platform for research on swallowing and dysphagia, as evidenced by a publication from DePippo. This journal encompasses a wide range of topics within the field of neurology, contributing to the understanding and treatment of neurological disorders."}{"title": "PERRY:"}{"title": "DEPIPPO:"}{"title": "BELAFSKY:Belafsky is a researcher who validated the Eating Assessment Tool-10 (EAT-10) in 2008."}{"title": "DRA. R. BURGOS:Dra. R. Burgos is a researcher who translated the EAT-10 into Spanish and contributed to its validation."}{"title": "EAT-10:The EAT-10, or Eating Assessment Tool-10, is a validated self-assessment questionnaire designed to evaluate the severity of swallowing problems, specifically dysphagia, experienced by patients. It serves as a screening tool to assess specific symptoms related to swallowing difficulties. The EAT-10 is recognized for its effectiveness in identifying dysphagia and is utilized in clinical settings to help healthcare professionals understand the extent of a patient's swallowing issues. This comprehensive tool is available in multiple languages, including Spanish, where it is referred to as \"test de cribado utilizado para evaluar la disfagia en el paciente.\" Overall, the EAT-10 is an essential instrument for evaluating and managing dysphagia in patients."}{"title": "UNIVERSIDAD DE SE\u00daL:The Universidad de Se\u00fal conducted a comprehensive study that reviewed various screening methods for dysphagia, significantly contributing to clinical practice. This review specifically examined 31 different screening methods for dysphagia that were developed and utilized between 1992 and 2011."}{"title": "GUSS:The Gugging Swallowing Assessment (GUSS) is a test that offers scientific rigor for detecting dysphagia."}{"title": "NUTR HOSP:NUTR HOSP is a specialized journal dedicated to the publication of articles and studies focused on nutrition within hospital settings. It encompasses a wide range of topics related to clinical nutrition research, including home artificial nutrition, enteral nutrition, and dietary requirements for older adults. The journal addresses various nutritional issues, such as the effectiveness of hypocaloric diets and the management of dysphagia, evidenced by its publication of the translation and validation of the EAT-10 scale for dysphagia screening.\n\nNUTR HOSP also explores the impact of nutrition on health, particularly concerning cardiovascular disease and obesity management. It publishes research that examines dietary modifications for patients and the overall effects of nutrition on health outcomes in hospital care. Through its comprehensive approach, NUTR HOSP serves as a vital resource for healthcare professionals interested in the intersection of nutrition and clinical practice."}{"title": "EUROPEAN SOCIETY FOR CLINICAL NUTRITION AND METABOLISM:The European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism (ESPEN) is a prominent organization dedicated to advancing the field of clinical nutrition and metabolism across Europe. It supports healthcare professionals by providing comprehensive guidelines and recommendations that are grounded in current research. ESPEN focuses on various aspects of clinical nutrition, including nutritional support in critical care settings, neurological pathologies, and specific patient populations such as those with dementia and liver disease.\n\nESPEN publishes guidelines that address nutritional assessment tools and practices, emphasizing the importance of enteral nutrition in clinical settings. The organization is committed to promoting best practices in clinical nutrition and metabolism, ensuring that healthcare providers have access to the latest evidence-based information to enhance patient care. Through its efforts, ESPEN plays a crucial role in shaping the standards and definitions related to nutritional support, thereby contributing significantly to the field of clinical nutrition and metabolism."}{"title": "SWALLOWING DISTURBANCE QUESTIONNAIRE:The Swallowing Disturbance Questionnaire is a tool recommended for screening swallowing disorders in patients with neurological conditions."}{"title": "DYSPHAGIA TEST-PARKINSON'S DISEASE:The Dysphagia Test for Parkinson's Disease is a screening tool specifically designed for assessing swallowing difficulties in Parkinson's patients."}{"title": "PATOLOG\u00cdAS NEUROL\u00d3GICAS:Neurological pathologies refer to a range of disorders affecting the nervous system, which can lead to complications such as dysphagia and malnutrition."}{"title": "CRIBADO DE LA DISFAGIA:Swallowing screening is a process used to identify patients at risk of dysphagia, particularly in those with neurological conditions."}{"title": "RECOMENDACIONES:The entity \"RECOMENDACIONES\" encompasses a set of guidelines designed to enhance clinical practices in various aspects of nutrition and health management. These recommendations are based on evidence and aim to improve dietary intake and nutritional needs across different age groups. Additionally, they provide specific guidance for the assessment and management of dysphagia, particularly in patients with neurological disorders. Overall, \"RECOMENDACIONES\" serves as a comprehensive framework for promoting optimal nutrition and health practices."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA:NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA is a dynamic and evolving discipline that focuses on the nutritional care and dietary management of patients, particularly in clinical settings. This field encompasses the assessment and management of dietary needs, nutritional therapy, and interventions aimed at improving health outcomes for individuals with various health conditions, including chronic illnesses, metabolic disorders, and those requiring specialized nutrition products.\n\nClinical nutrition involves the study and application of nutrition principles in the context of health and disease management, emphasizing the importance of dietary interventions in the prevention and treatment of diseases. It includes practices such as the use of parenteral nutrition for patients with specific needs, dietary modifications for individuals with swallowing difficulties, and nutritional support for patients with conditions like cancer, burns, and severe trauma.\n\nNUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA also highlights the design and development of clinical nutrition products, which is a comprehensive process that involves generating ideas, conducting formulation trials, and ensuring that these products meet specific health and dietary requirements. This aspect of clinical nutrition is crucial for providing essential nutrients to patients and improving their overall health.\n\nFurthermore, NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA is integrated into evidence-based medicine, focusing on the nutritional needs of patients and the application of nutritional knowledge in clinical decision-making processes. It plays a vital role in the management of patients' dietary needs, particularly in hospital settings, and is increasingly supported by research aimed at enhancing patient outcomes through effective dietary management and interventions."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL:NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL is a vital method of delivering nutrition directly to the gastrointestinal tract, primarily designed for patients who are unable to consume food orally. This approach is often favored over parenteral nutrition due to its physiological benefits, safety, and efficacy. It involves administering nutrients either orally or through a feeding tube directly into the stomach or intestines, making it suitable for a variety of patient populations, including those with swallowing difficulties, chronic illnesses, or post-surgical needs.\n\nThis method is particularly beneficial for critically ill patients, individuals with severe dysphagia, and those with conditions that impair nutrient absorption, such as cystic fibrosis or pancreatitis. It is also extensively utilized in pediatric care, especially for premature infants, to ensure adequate growth and development. NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL helps maintain the integrity of the intestinal barrier, reduces the risk of infections, and improves overall nutritional status.\n\nIn clinical settings, enteral nutrition is typically initiated when oral intake is insufficient, often starting 5-7 days before surgery and continuing postoperatively. It is tailored to meet individual caloric and nutritional needs, utilizing specially formulated diets. However, it may present complications, such as digestive symptoms or increased infection risk, necessitating careful management to avoid interactions with medications.\n\nNUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL serves as a critical intervention for patients who cannot meet their nutritional requirements through traditional means, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients to support their health and recovery. It is particularly indicated for patients with conditions like neoplasia, fistulas, and Crohn's disease, and is essential for maintaining digestive tract integrity and minimizing inflammatory responses. Overall, this nutritional support method has developed significantly in recent years and is preferred when the digestive tract is functional, making it a cornerstone of modern nutritional therapy."}{"title": "GASTROSTOM\u00cdA PERCUT\u00c1NEA ENDOSC\u00d3PICA:La gastrostom\u00eda percut\u00e1nea endosc\u00f3pica es un procedimiento para administrar nutrici\u00f3n enteral en pacientes con dificultades para alimentarse."}{"title": "CRIBADO:CRIBADO refers to a screening process that involves evaluating individuals to detect various health conditions. This process is particularly important for identifying issues such as dysphagia in patients suffering from multiple sclerosis and stroke. Additionally, screening is utilized to test for diseases in individuals who do not yet exhibit symptoms. Furthermore, the CRIBADO process serves as a method to assess patients for nutritional risk prior to undergoing surgical interventions. Overall, CRIBADO encompasses a comprehensive approach to early detection and risk assessment in healthcare."}{"title": "RECOMENDACI\u00d3N:Las recomendaciones son gu\u00edas establecidas para el manejo de la nutrici\u00f3n y la disfagia en pacientes con esclerosis m\u00faltiple e ictus."}{"title": "VIDEOFLOROSCOPIA:VIDEOFLOROSCOPIA is an instrumental technique utilized to assess swallowing function in patients with dysphagia, particularly beneficial for those exhibiting early signs of swallowing difficulties. This diagnostic procedure involves the observation of the passage of food or liquid through the oropharynx using fluoroscopy, allowing for a detailed evaluation of swallowing mechanics. It is typically performed in specialized settings, ensuring that patients receive accurate assessments and appropriate interventions for their swallowing issues."}{"title": "M\u00c9TODO DE EXPLORACI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA VOLUMEN-VISCOSIDAD (MECV-V):El MECV-V es una herramienta que ayuda a detectar alteraciones en la degluci\u00f3n y determina la viscosidad y volumen adecuados para pacientes con disfagia."}{"title": "VELASCO M:Velasco M es uno de los autores que contribuy\u00f3 a la gu\u00eda de diagn\u00f3stico y tratamiento nutricional y rehabilitador de la disfagia orofar\u00edngea."}{"title": "SHU-YING FU:Shu-Ying Fu is an author who contributed to the systematic review on the validity and reliability of swallowing screening tools used by nurses for dysphagia."}{"title": "WAN-HSIANG WANG:Wan-Hsiang Wang is an author who contributed to the systematic review on the validity and reliability of swallowing screening tools used by nurses for dysphagia."}{"title": "YU-CHIN MA:Yu-Chin Ma is an author who contributed to the systematic review on the validity and reliability of swallowing screening tools used by nurses for dysphagia."}{"title": "DE PIPPO KL:De Pippo KL is an author who validated the Burke dysphagia screening test for patients with stroke."}{"title": "HOLAS MA:Holas MA is an author who validated the Burke dysphagia screening test for patients with stroke."}{"title": "REDING MJ:Reding MJ is an author who validated the Burke dysphagia screening test for patients with stroke."}{"title": "TRAPL M:Trapl M is an author who contributed to the study of the Gugging Swallowing Screen."}{"title": "ENDERLE P:Enderle P is an author who contributed to the study of the Gugging Swallowing Screen."}{"title": "NOWOTNY M:Nowotny M is an author who contributed to the study of the Gugging Swallowing Screen."}{"title": "ABDELHAMID AHMED:AbdelHamid Ahmed is an author who applied the GUSS test on adult Egyptian dysphagic patients."}{"title": "ABO-HASSEBA AHMED:Abo-Hasseba Ahmed is an author who applied the GUSS test on adult Egyptian dysphagic patients."}{"title": "SILVER F:Silver F is an author who developed and validated the Toronto Bedside Swallowing Screening Test (TOR-BSST) for patients with stroke."}{"title": "TEASELL R:Teasell R is an author who developed and validated the Toronto Bedside Swallowing Screening Test (TOR-BSST) for patients with stroke."}{"title": "BAYLEY M:Bayley M is an author who developed and validated the Toronto Bedside Swallowing Screening Test (TOR-BSST) for patients with stroke."}{"title": "EDMIASTON J:Edmiaston J is an author who contributed to the development of a simple bedside stroke dysphagia screen."}{"title": "CONNOR LT:Connor LT is an author who contributed to the development of a simple bedside stroke dysphagia screen."}{"title": "STEGER-MAY K:Steger-May K is an author who contributed to the development of a simple bedside stroke dysphagia screen."}{"title": "FORD AL:Ford AL is an author who contributed to the development of a simple bedside stroke dysphagia screen."}{"title": "MCHORNEY CA:McHorney CA is an author recognized for developing the SWAL-QOL and SWAL-CARE outcomes tools, which are specifically designed to assess oropharyngeal dysphagia in adults. These tools play a significant role in evaluating the quality of life and care related to swallowing disorders."}{"title": "BRICKER DE:Bricker DE is an author who developed the SWAL-QOL outcomes tool for oropharyngeal dysphagia in adults."}{"title": "KRAMER AE:Kramer AE is an author who developed the SWAL-QOL outcomes tool for oropharyngeal dysphagia in adults."}{"title": "BALLASTEROS MD:Ballesteros MD is an author who discussed nutritional strategies for patients after a stroke."}{"title": "PALAZUELO L:Palazuelo L is an author who discussed nutritional strategies for patients after a stroke."}{"title": "ETGES CL:Etges CL is an author who conducted a systematic review on screening tools for dysphagia."}{"title": "BURGOS R:Burgos R is a researcher who has made significant contributions to the field of malnutrition, particularly focusing on diabetic patients. In addition to their research work, Burgos R is also an author known for translating and validating the EAT-10 scale, which is utilized for dysphagia screening. This dual role highlights Burgos R's commitment to improving health outcomes through both research and practical assessment tools in the medical community."}{"title": "PARK YH:Park YH is an author who conducted a systematic review on dysphagia screening measures for use in nursing homes."}{"title": "ESPEN:ESPEN, which stands for the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism, is a prominent organization dedicated to advancing the study and practice of clinical nutrition and metabolism across Europe. It provides comprehensive guidelines and recommendations for various aspects of clinical nutrition, including enteral and parenteral nutrition, aimed at improving patient care in diverse medical settings.\n\nESPEN develops and disseminates clinical guidelines for nutritional support tailored to specific patient populations, including critically ill patients, those undergoing surgery, oncology patients, and individuals with conditions such as liver disease, pancreatitis, and renal insufficiency. The organization emphasizes the importance of nutritional screening and assessment, recommending tools like the Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool (MUST) and the Mini Nutritional Assessment (MNA) for identifying malnutrition risk, particularly in elderly and frail individuals.\n\nIn addition to its focus on clinical guidelines, ESPEN supports projects addressing hospital malnutrition and offers scholarships to enhance nutritional practices in healthcare settings. The organization also provides recommendations for nutritional interventions in patients with special needs, such as those with dementia, and promotes the use of immunomodulatory formulas for patients undergoing cancer surgery.\n\nESPEN's guidelines cover a wide range of topics, including preoperative nutritional support, management of acute intestinal failure, and hydration relevant to diabetes management. The organization is committed to evidence-based practices and regularly publishes consensus papers and research findings to inform healthcare professionals about the latest developments in clinical nutrition.\n\nOverall, ESPEN plays a crucial role in shaping the standards of nutritional care in Europe, ensuring that healthcare providers have access to the latest evidence and recommendations to support their patients' nutritional needs effectively."}{"title": "GIL A:Gil A is an author of the \"Tratado de Nutrici\u00f3n\" which discusses various aspects of nutrition."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N Y DISFAGIA:Nutrici\u00f3n y disfagia is a topic discussed in the context of managing dysphagia through nutritional strategies.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "VIDEOENDOSCOPIA DE LA DEGLUCI\u00d3N:The \"VIDEOENDOSCOPIA DE LA DEGLUCI\u00d3N\" is a diagnostic procedure that allows for the observation of the swallowing phase in patients, which is crucial for diagnosing oropharyngeal dysphagia. This technique involves both static and dynamic assessments of the anatomical structures involved in the swallowing process. It was first described by Dr. Susan Langmore in 1988 and is utilized to evaluate swallowing function and anatomy in patients experiencing difficulties with swallowing. The procedure is conducted in specialized units, such as the UFDOF unit, ensuring a comprehensive evaluation of the patient's swallowing capabilities."}{"title": "OTORRINOLARING\u00d3LOGO:An otolaryngologist is a medical specialist responsible for diagnosing and treating conditions related to the ear, nose, and throat, including dysphagia."}{"title": "TRATADO DE NUTRICI\u00d3N:The \"TRATADO DE NUTRICI\u00d3N\" is a comprehensive work on nutrition that was published in 2017 by Editorial M\u00e9dica Panamericana. Edited by Gil Hern\u00e1ndez, this publication covers various aspects of dietary science, providing an in-depth exploration of nutritional principles and practices."}{"title": "VIDEOENDOSCOPIA:Videoendoscopia is a diagnostic procedure that employs videoendoscopy, an instrumental technique, to visualize the swallowing process and assess dysphagia. This method is specifically designed to evaluate swallowing function in patients experiencing difficulties, providing valuable insights into their condition."}{"title": "VIDEOFLOUROSCOPIA DE LA DEGLUCI\u00d3N:Videofluoroscopy of swallowing is a diagnostic imaging technique that evaluates the swallowing process in real-time."}{"title": "EDITORIAL M\u00c9DICA PANAMERICANA:Editorial M\u00e9dica Panamericana is a publishing house known for its contributions to medical literature. It is particularly recognized for publishing the \"Tratado de Nutrici\u00f3n,\" a comprehensive medical textbook that discusses oligomonomeric formulas among other topics related to nutrition."}{"title": "EUROPEAN SOCIETY FOR SWALLOWING DISORDERS:The European Society for Swallowing Disorders (ESSD) is an organization dedicated to advancing research and education concerning swallowing disorders, particularly dysphagia. In 2012, the ESSD played a pivotal role by hosting a meeting that initiated the International Dysphagia Diet Standardisation Initiative (IDDSI), aimed at standardizing practices related to dysphagia management. Additionally, the ESSD is committed to providing guidelines and standards for the diagnosis and treatment of swallowing disorders, ensuring that healthcare professionals have access to the most current and effective practices in the field."}{"title": "SUSAN LANGMORE:Dr. Susan Langmore is a physician known for her contributions to the evaluation of swallowing disorders and for publishing a key reference book on the subject in 2001."}{"title": "VFS:VFS, or Videofluoroscopic Swallowing Study, is a diagnostic procedure utilized to analyze the swallowing process and the movement of anatomical structures involved in bolus formation and propulsion. It is specifically designed to observe the oral phase of swallowing and is regarded as the gold standard in diagnosing swallowing disorders. The procedure involves a radiological examination that provides detailed insights into the mechanics of swallowing, making it an essential tool for healthcare professionals in assessing and treating patients with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "VED:VED, or Videofluoroscopic Esophageal Dysphagia, is a diagnostic test utilized to evaluate the swallowing process, particularly focusing on the pharyngeal phase of swallowing. This test assesses both the oral phase and the function of the upper esophageal sphincter. VED serves as an exploration process in a medical context, specifically aimed at assessing swallowing and the anatomical structures involved. Additionally, it is often performed in conjunction with videoendoscopy (VFS) to provide a comprehensive evaluation of swallowing function."}{"title": "FIBROSCOPIOS:Fibroscopes are medical instruments used by otolaryngologists for endoscopic examinations, including the evaluation of swallowing."}{"title": "MANOMETR\u00cdA ESOF\u00c1GICA:MANOMETR\u00cdA ESOF\u00c1GICA is a diagnostic test that measures the pressure and coordination of muscle contractions in the esophagus. This procedure is essential for assessing swallowing disorders and diagnosing esophageal motility disorders. By evaluating the pressure patterns and muscle activity within the esophagus, MANOMETR\u00cdA ESOF\u00c1GICA provides critical insights into the functioning of this vital organ."}{"title": "PH-METR\u00cdA DE 24 HORAS:24-hour pH monitoring is a diagnostic test used to measure acid levels in the esophagus, which can help identify issues related to swallowing."}{"title": "IMPEDANCIOMETR\u00cdA INTRALUMINAL:Intraluminal impedance is a diagnostic test that measures the flow of liquids and solids in the esophagus, aiding in the evaluation of swallowing disorders."}{"title": "OTORRINOLARING\u00d3LOGOS:OTORRINOLARING\u00d3LOGOS, also known as otolaryngologists, are medical specialists dedicated to the diagnosis and treatment of disorders associated with the head and neck. Their expertise encompasses a range of conditions related to the ear, nose, and throat, including specific issues such as oropharyngeal dysphagia, which refers to swallowing disorders. These professionals play a crucial role in evaluating and managing various ailments affecting the throat and surrounding areas, ensuring comprehensive care for patients with related health concerns."}{"title": "LANGMORE:LANGMORE refers to both Dr. Langmore, a medical professional recognized for her expertise in swallowing disorders, and a scale developed for assessing the risk of aspiration in patients. Dr. Langmore is particularly noted for her contributions to the field, including the publication of a reference manual on swallowing disorders in 2001. The Langmore scale serves as a tool for evaluating the risk of aspiration by analyzing the occupation of pharyngeal-laryngeal areas by secretions, thereby aiding in the clinical assessment of patients with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "ENDOSCOPIC EVALUATION AND TREATMENT OF SWALLOWING DISORDERS:A book published by Dr. Langmore in 2001 that serves as a reference for diagnosing and treating swallowing disorders."}{"title": "VIDEOENDOSCOPIC EXPLORATION:A procedure similar to that proposed by Dr. Langmore, used to evaluate swallowing by observing anatomy and swallowing mechanics."}{"title": "METHEMOGLOBINEMIA:A medical condition that can occur due to the use of certain dyes, such as methylene blue, during swallowing evaluations."}{"title": "VIDEOENDOSCOPE:A medical device used in the videoendoscopic exploration to visualize the anatomy and assess swallowing."}{"title": "HIGH DEFINITION SCREEN:A display device used in conjunction with a videoendoscope to provide clear images during swallowing evaluations."}{"title": "CONSENT FORM:A document that patients must sign to acknowledge understanding of the risks associated with swallowing evaluations."}{"title": "THICKENING AGENT:A substance used to modify the consistency of liquids for swallowing evaluations, ensuring safety for patients with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "SWALLOWING DISORDERS:"}{"title": "PACIENTE:The entity \"PACIENTE\" refers to individuals receiving medical care, particularly those with specific health conditions that necessitate various forms of treatment and nutritional support. In the context of oropharyngeal dysphagia, a patient is someone who experiences difficulties with swallowing and may require assistance during meals to prevent choking and ensure proper nutrition. This includes individuals undergoing evaluation and treatment for swallowing disorders, who receive care from a multidisciplinary team at specialized units.\n\nPatients may also be those receiving medical treatment for complications related to catheter use, nutritional risks associated with surgery, or conditions such as cancer, diabetes, and other critical illnesses. They often require tailored dietary modifications due to challenges in chewing or swallowing, and their nutritional needs are assessed to determine appropriate enteral or parenteral nutrition.\n\nSpecific cases include patients diagnosed with conditions such as adenocarcinoma of the pancreas, severe caloric malnutrition, and various eating disorders, who may experience significant weight loss and require specialized interventions. For instance, individuals with diabetes, including type 1 and type 2, may face challenges in managing their insulin intake and dietary habits, while those with cystic fibrosis or Crohn's disease may undergo multiple nutritional therapies and surgeries.\n\nAdditionally, patients may be monitored for complications arising from their conditions, such as diarrhea or fluctuations in glucose levels, and they have rights regarding their medical information and consent for treatment. The importance of patient collaboration during procedures, such as the placement of a nasogastric tube, is also emphasized.\n\nOverall, \"PACIENTE\" encompasses a diverse group of individuals who are actively engaged in their healthcare, receiving various forms of nutritional support and medical treatment tailored to their unique health challenges."}{"title": "VIDEOENDOSCOPIO:The videoendoscope is a medical instrument used to visualize the anatomical structures during the VED process."}{"title": "BASE DE LA LENGUA:The base of the tongue is an anatomical area assessed for its function in swallowing during the VED."}{"title": "PAQUIDERMIA INTERARITENOIDEA:Paquidermia interaritenoidea is an indirect sign of reflux that can affect swallowing sensitivity and is evaluated during the VED process."}{"title": "CONSTRICTORES FAR\u00cdNGEOS:The constrictores far\u00edngeos are muscles involved in swallowing that are activated during the assessment process."}{"title": "MANIOBRA DE VALSALVA:The maniobra de Valsalva is a maneuver performed by the patient to assess the function of the laryngeal structures during the VED."}{"title": "FONEMAS VELARES OCLUSIVOS:The fonemas velares oclusivos are specific sounds used during the assessment to evaluate the mobility of the velum."}{"title": "DEGLUCIONES SECAS:Degluciones secas refer to the dry swallows performed by the patient, which are observed during the VED to assess swallowing function."}{"title": "JONATHAN AVIV:Jonathan Aviv is a researcher who published a new method for sensory evaluation in swallowing in 1998, known as FEESST."}{"title": "FEESST:FEESST stands for Flexible Endoscopic Evaluation of Swallowing with Sensory Testing, a method developed to assess swallowing reflexes using air impulses."}{"title": "LANGMORE SCALE:The Langmore scale is a published scale used to quantify the degree of occupation of pharyngeal areas with a patient's own secretions."}{"title": "MURRAY SCALE:The Murray scale is another published scale used for assessing the risk of aspiration based on secretions in the pharyngeal areas."}{"title": "LARYNX:The larynx is a critical area in swallowing, involved in protecting the airway and facilitating sound production."}{"title": "DEGLUTITION:Deglutition refers to the act of swallowing, which is a complex process involving various anatomical structures."}{"title": "XEROSTOMIA:Xerostomia is a condition characterized by dry mouth due to reduced saliva production, which can affect swallowing."}{"title": "ALHAMIA PRISON:Alhamia Prison is a facility located in Tiruzia, known for holding various individuals, including hostages and prisoners such as Samuel Namara. The prison is relevant to multiple medical contexts, including discussions surrounding hypopituitarism, malnutrition among prisoners, and the treatment of conditions like precocious puberty. It has been mentioned in relation to evaluating swallowing and related functions, as well as in the context of medical observation or treatment for complications arising from procedures like GEP. Additionally, Alhamia Prison has been inferred to have significance in discussions about hyperprolactinemia in men, particularly concerning the health and fragility of elderly inmates. Overall, the facility serves as a critical point of reference for various medical and health-related issues affecting those held within its walls."}{"title": "ENDOSCOPE:"}{"title": "MURRAY:Murray is another scale published for assessing the degree of secretion occupation in pharyngeal areas."}{"title": "ICE CHIP PROTOCOL:The Ice Chip Protocol is a method recommended for patients with poor management of secretions, involving the administration of small ice fragments to stimulate swallowing."}{"title": "HYPOPHARYNX:The hypopharynx is an anatomical area that includes the piriform sinuses and retrocricoid area where secretions can also accumulate."}{"title": "LARYNGEAL VESTIBULE:The laryngeal vestibule is an anatomical area where secretions can be present during swallowing evaluations."}{"title": "SWALLOWING EVALUATION:Swallowing evaluation is a process that assesses the patient's ability to swallow safely and effectively, often involving various textures and volumes of food."}{"title": "TEXTURE N\u00c9CTAR:Nectar is a type of food consistency used in swallowing evaluations, characterized as an intermediate consistency."}{"title": "PUDDING:Pudding is a type of food consistency used in swallowing evaluations, characterized as a high consistency."}{"title": "LIQUID:Liquid is a type of food consistency used in swallowing evaluations, characterized as a thin consistency."}{"title": "SOLID FOOD:Solid food is a type of food consistency that is evaluated during swallowing assessments, requiring competent dentition for safe consumption."}{"title": "ALBONDIGA EN SALSA:Alb\u00f3ndiga en salsa is an example of solid food that can be evaluated for swallowing, which can be mashed with a fork and served with sauce."}{"title": "DENTITION:Dentition refers to the condition of a patient's teeth, which is crucial for evaluating their ability to swallow solid foods."}{"title": "OROPHARYNX:"}{"title": "VIDEOFLUOROSCOPIA DE LA DEGLUCI\u00d3N:A radiographic procedure designed to define the anatomy and physiology of swallowing in patients and to examine the effectiveness of rehabilitation strategies."}{"title": "LOGOPEDA:A logopeda, also known as a logopedist or speech therapist, is a specialized professional dedicated to improving oral and swallowing functions in patients. They conduct various exercises and therapies aimed at enhancing speech and language abilities, as well as addressing swallowing disorders such as dysphagia. In particular, logopedas play a crucial role in the rehabilitation process for individuals experiencing swallowing difficulties. They also work with children to rehabilitate swallowing and feeding behaviors, helping to normalize oral stimulation. Overall, the logopeda's expertise encompasses a wide range of speech and language therapy, making them essential in the treatment and support of patients with communication and swallowing challenges."}{"title": "EQUIPAMIENTO:The basic fluoroscopic unit required for conducting swallowing assessments, including a constant radiation source and a radiography detector."}{"title": "ANATOM\u00cdA:The study of the structure of the body, particularly relevant in understanding the swallowing process in patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "FISIOLOG\u00cdA:Fisiolog\u00eda refers to the study of bodily functions and processes, encompassing various aspects of human health and performance. It is particularly relevant in the context of nutrition and exercise performance, as it helps to understand how the body responds to different dietary and physical activities. Additionally, Fisiolog\u00eda includes the examination of specific functions such as swallowing and dysphagia, highlighting its importance in understanding both general bodily functions and specific health conditions."}{"title": "T\u00c9CNICAS DE MEJORA SENSORIAL:Techniques used to enhance sensory feedback during swallowing assessments and rehabilitation."}{"title": "MANIOBRAS DE DEGLUCI\u00d3N:Specific maneuvers employed to improve swallowing safety and efficacy during assessments and treatments."}{"title": "RADIACI\u00d3N:Radiation refers to the exposure of patients to radiation during medical procedures, with specific criteria for justification, optimization, and limitation of exposure."}{"title": "C\u00c1MARA:The camera is a device used in the VFS to visualize the radiographic images on a monitor for recording purposes."}{"title": "EQUIPO DE ATENCI\u00d3N M\u00c9DICA:The medical care team is responsible for conducting the VFS and ensuring the safety of both the patient and themselves during the procedure."}{"title": "COLIMADOR:A collimator is a device used to limit the size and shape of the X-ray beam in radiographic systems."}{"title": "TUBO DE RAYOS:The X-ray tube is a component of the radiographic system that generates X-rays for imaging purposes during the VFS."}{"title": "SILLAS ESPECIALIZADAS:Specialized chairs are designed to fit between the table and the image intensifier, facilitating patient positioning during the VFS."}{"title": "MANTO DE PROTECCI\u00d3N:A protective gown used to shield patients, especially children, from radiation exposure during medical procedures."}{"title": "COLLAR DE TIROIDES:A thyroid collar is a protective device worn by medical staff to shield the thyroid gland from radiation during imaging procedures."}{"title": "DELANTAL DE PLOMO:A lead apron is worn by medical personnel to protect against radiation exposure during procedures like the VFS."}{"title": "GAFAS PROTECTORAS:Protective glasses worn by medical staff to shield their eyes from radiation during imaging procedures."}{"title": "FLUOROSCOPIA:"}{"title": "ESCALA DE PENETRACI\u00d3N-ASPIRACI\u00d3N DE ROSENBECK:A scale developed by Rosenbeck in 1996 to assess the severity of airway penetration and aspiration during swallowing."}{"title": "C1:C1 refers to the first cervical vertebra, which is relevant in the context of pharyngeal contraction during swallowing."}{"title": "V\u00cdA A\u00c9REA:V\u00cdA A\u00c9REA refers to the airway, which is the passage that connects the nose and mouth to the lungs. This structure is essential for proper respiratory function and plays a critical role in swallowing safety. Issues related to swallowing can significantly impact the airway, potentially leading to complications. Therefore, maintaining the integrity of the airway is vital for both breathing and safe swallowing."}{"title": "BOL:BOL refers to the bolus, which is a mass of food or liquid formed in the mouth and subsequently swallowed. This process can be influenced by the viscosity of thickeners, which may alter the consistency of the bolus. The bolus plays a significant role in the study of swallowing mechanics, as it is the key element that is swallowed during the act of eating or drinking."}{"title": "VALL\u00c9CULA:The vallecula is a space at the back of the throat that plays a role in swallowing and can be a site for food residue."}{"title": "ESF\u00cdNTER ESOF\u00c1GICO:The esophageal sphincter is a muscle that controls the passage of food from the esophagus into the stomach, important for swallowing safety."}{"title": "MOVIMIENTO HIOIDEO:Hyoid movement refers to the motion of the hyoid bone during swallowing, which is essential for the proper function of the swallowing mechanism."}{"title": "EXCURSI\u00d3N LAR\u00cdNGEA:Laryngeal excursion is the upward and forward movement of the larynx during swallowing, crucial for airway protection."}{"title": "PENETRACI\u00d3N:Penetration is the entry of material into the airway above the vocal cords during swallowing, which can lead to aspiration if not managed properly."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES DE LA SEGURIDAD:Safety alterations refer to changes in swallowing that increase the risk of penetration or aspiration."}{"title": "OMNIPAQUE:Omnipaque is a non-ionic, monomeric, tri-iodinated, water-soluble radiological contrast medium used in diagnostic imaging."}{"title": "ESF\u00cdNTER ESOF\u00c1GICO SUPERIOR:The \"ESF\u00cdNTER ESOF\u00c1GICO SUPERIOR\" is a muscle that plays a crucial role in controlling the entry of food into the esophagus. It is a functional unit involved in the process of swallowing, consisting of muscles that regulate the passage of food. This sphincter is particularly significant in the evaluation of oropharyngeal dysphagia, a condition that affects the ability to swallow."}{"title": "PRUEBAS DIAGN\u00d3STICAS INSTRUMENTALES:Instrumental diagnostic tests are used to evaluate swallowing and identify any dysfunctions or abnormalities."}{"title": "RESIDUO:The term \"RESIDUO\" refers to the materials that remain in the body after the process of digestion, which can be significant in diagnostic studies of the digestive tract. Additionally, \"residue\" also pertains to the leftover food or liquid present in the pharynx following swallowing, which may indicate potential difficulties in swallowing. This dual definition highlights the importance of residue in both digestive health and the assessment of swallowing function."}{"title": "FASES DE LA DEGLUCI\u00d3N:The phases of swallowing include oral, pharyngeal, and esophageal phases, each critical for effective swallowing."}{"title": "ENFERMEDADES NEUROMUSCULARES:ENFERMEDADES NEUROMUSCULARES refers to a category of diseases that impact the muscles and their direct nervous control. These conditions may necessitate specialized nutritional approaches, particularly in pediatric care, to support the health and development of affected individuals."}{"title": "CIPLINARES:Ciplinare is an organization involved in the analysis and diagnosis of swallowing phases using instrumental tests."}{"title": "PHARYNGEAL PHASE:The pharyngeal phase is the stage of swallowing that follows the oral phase, involving the movement of the bolus through the pharynx."}{"title": "APRAKSI:Apraxia is a condition that affects the ability to manage the bolus in the oral cavity."}{"title": "SCALE OF YALE:The Yale Pharyngeal Residue Severity Rating Scale is used to evaluate the residue that persists after swallowing."}{"title": "ROSENBECK SCALE:The Rosenbeck scale is used to describe the degree of penetration or aspiration during swallowing."}{"title": "ORAL PHASE:"}{"title": "YALE SCALE:A standardized scale developed for assessing the severity of pharyngeal residue after swallowing, providing a reliable anatomical evaluation based on imaging."}{"title": "VIDEOFLUOROSCOPY (VFS):A diagnostic imaging technique used to visualize the swallowing process and assess the presence of residue and aspiration."}{"title": "VIDEOENDOSCOPY:A technique for static and dynamic evaluation of the structures involved in swallowing, used to assess secretions and other abnormalities."}{"title": "CRICOPHARYNGEAL DYSFUNCTION:A common pathological finding related to the inability of the upper esophageal sphincter to relax and distend, potentially leading to swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "VALORACI\u00d3N DE SENSIBILIDAD Y SECRECIONES:An assessment method discussed in the manual that evaluates sensitivity and secretions related to swallowing."}{"title": "SENSIBILIDAD:SENSIBILIDAD refers to the assessment of sensitivity in various medical contexts. In the realm of swallowing disorders, it pertains to the evaluation of sensitivity as outlined in relevant manuals. Additionally, SENSIBILIDAD is associated with the ability of diagnostic tests to accurately identify patients with pheochromocytomas, a type of tumor that can affect the adrenal glands. This sensitivity can vary depending on the imaging techniques employed. Specifically, tests such as 18F-FDG and MIBG are noted for their sensitivity in detecting the presence of disease, including metastatic pheochromocytomas. Overall, SENSIBILIDAD encompasses both the evaluation of swallowing disorders and the effectiveness of imaging tests in identifying specific medical conditions."}{"title": "SECRECIONES:Refers to the evaluation of secretions that may affect swallowing, as discussed in the manual."}{"title": "FASE ESOF\u00c1GICA:The esophageal phase of swallowing, which is evaluated directly and indirectly in the context of dysphagia."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES DE LA COLUMNA CERVICAL:Refers to cervical spine abnormalities that can impact swallowing mechanics, as mentioned in the manual."}{"title": "RESIDUO FAR\u00cdNGEO:"}{"title": "ESOFAOGOSCOPIA TRANSNASAL:Esofagoscopia transnasal is a technique that allows for examination of the esophagus through the nasal cavity without the need for sedation."}{"title": "CUERPOS DE CUIDADOS INTENSIVOS:Unidades de cuidados intensivos are specialized hospital departments that provide intensive care for patients who are critically ill."}{"title": "TOXINA:Toxina refers to substances that may be used in various therapeutic techniques mentioned in the manual for treating esophageal conditions."}{"title": "DILATACI\u00d3N ESOF\u00c1GICA:Dilataci\u00f3n esof\u00e1gica is a procedure performed to widen the esophagus, often discussed in the context of treating dysphagia."}{"title": "BIOPSIAS:Biopsias, also known as biopsies, are medical procedures that involve the removal of tissue samples for examination. These procedures are crucial diagnostic techniques used to identify diseases, including conditions such as FQ. By sampling tissue, biopsias allow healthcare professionals to analyze the cellular structure and determine the presence of any abnormalities or diseases."}{"title": "GASTROSTOM\u00cdA PERCUT\u00c1NEA:Gastrostom\u00eda percut\u00e1nea is a procedure for placing a feeding tube directly into the stomach, relevant in the context of dysphagia treatment."}{"title": "PUNCIONES TRAQUEOESOF\u00c1GICAS:Punciones traqueoesof\u00e1gicas are procedures that may be performed to address complications related to esophageal conditions.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "REFLUJO GASTROESOF\u00c1GICO:El reflujo gastroesof\u00e1gico (RGE) es una afecci\u00f3n multifactorial que se caracteriza por la exposici\u00f3n del es\u00f3fago distal al \u00e1cido, lo que puede provocar molestias y complicaciones. Esta condici\u00f3n, tambi\u00e9n conocida como enfermedad por reflujo gastroesof\u00e1gico (GERD), es un trastorno digestivo cr\u00f3nico en el que el \u00e1cido del est\u00f3mago o la bilis irritan el revestimiento del es\u00f3fago. El RGE es prevalente entre los pacientes con fibrosis qu\u00edstica, donde un porcentaje significativo experimenta s\u00edntomas relacionados. Adem\u00e1s, se ha observado que el reflujo gastroesof\u00e1gico puede empeorar o ser inducido por procedimientos de gastrostom\u00eda. En resumen, el REFLUJO GASTROESOF\u00c1GICO es una condici\u00f3n que genera altos costes sanitarios y requiere atenci\u00f3n m\u00e9dica adecuada para su manejo."}{"title": "ES\u00d3FAGO DE BARRETT:El es\u00f3fago de Barrett es una condici\u00f3n precancerosa asociada al reflujo gastroesof\u00e1gico que requiere diagn\u00f3stico y tratamiento."}{"title": "PH-METR\u00cdA ESOF\u00c1GICA:La pH-metr\u00eda esof\u00e1gica es una prueba diagn\u00f3stica que cuantifica el reflujo \u00e1cido y es la prueba de referencia para el diagn\u00f3stico de la enfermedad por reflujo gastroesof\u00e1gico."}{"title": "IBP:IBP, or Inhibitors of Proton Pump, is a class of medications utilized to treat acid-related conditions, particularly gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD) and esophagitis. These medications are effective in alleviating symptoms associated with gastroesophageal reflux, making them a common choice for managing these conditions. In summary, IBP medications play a crucial role in the treatment of GERD and related disorders."}{"title": "ANEMIA:Anemia is a common medical condition characterized by a deficiency of red blood cells or hemoglobin in the blood, leading to symptoms such as fatigue and weakness. It is often associated with various underlying health issues, including Wilson's disease, where it may result from hemolysis and liver dysfunction. Anemia can arise from multiple causes, including iron deficiency, chronic diseases, malabsorption, and nutrient deficiencies, particularly in conditions like inflammatory bowel diseases and celiac disease. In celiac patients, iron deficiency anemia is frequently observed due to malabsorption of nutrients, including iron and folic acid.\n\nThe condition can also be prevalent among malnourished elderly individuals and cancer patients. In chronic kidney disease, anemia may occur due to a lack of erythropoietin, a hormone essential for red blood cell production. Additionally, anemia can be linked to disorders of iron metabolism, such as hereditary hemochromatosis, and can be managed through dietary control of iron intake.\n\nAnemia is not only a sign of potential nutritional deficiencies but can also indicate more serious underlying conditions, necessitating further evaluation, especially in patients presenting atypical symptoms. Overall, anemia is a multifaceted condition that requires careful assessment and management based on its diverse causes and implications for health."}{"title": "P\u00c9RDIDA DE PESO:\"P\u00c9RDIDA DE PESO\" refers to the significant reduction in body weight experienced by patients, which is a critical indicator of malnutrition and is often evaluated to determine nutritional status. This condition can manifest as a weight loss of 5 kg or more over a period of six months, with percentages of weight loss ranging from 13% to 17%. It is particularly concerning in patients with specific health conditions, such as gastroesophageal reflux disease, where it may indicate potential complications, and in cancer patients, where it is commonly associated with malnutrition and caquexia.\n\nIn geriatric patients, weight loss can also signify malnutrition and is a common symptom that necessitates further investigation. The assessment of weight loss is crucial in various medical contexts, including the management of patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (EPOC), where it may relate to malnutrition and increased energy expenditure. Additionally, weight loss is a monitored outcome in neonates, especially regarding fluid management and overall health assessment.\n\nOverall, \"P\u00c9RDIDA DE PESO\" is a significant health concern that is systematically measured and classified according to its severity, serving as a vital parameter in diagnosing malnutrition and assessing the overall health status of patients across different medical conditions."}{"title": "TOS CR\u00d3NICA:La tos cr\u00f3nica puede ser un s\u00edntoma at\u00edpico de reflujo gastroesof\u00e1gico y requiere evaluaci\u00f3n para determinar su causa."}Ä2␀␀␀␀␀y2␀␀␀␀␀e$2␀␀␀␀␀d&2␀␀␀␀␀ü*2␀␀␀␀␀y,2␀␀␀␀␀-2␀␀␀␀␀∞-2␀␀␀␀␀˜32␀␀␀␀␀ô42␀␀␀␀␀ 72␀␀␀␀␀ÓA2␀␀␀␀␀xG2␀␀␀␀␀£G2␀␀␀␀␀ﬂJ2␀␀␀␀␀áK2␀␀␀␀␀L2␀␀␀␀␀M2␀␀␀␀␀îV2␀␀␀␀␀é^2␀␀␀␀␀a2␀␀␀␀␀ d2␀␀␀␀␀∏f2␀␀␀␀␀ah2␀␀␀␀␀‡k2␀␀␀␀␀up2␀␀␀␀␀4u2␀␀␀␀␀‡u2␀␀␀␀␀÷y2␀␀␀␀␀Ä2␀␀␀␀␀–á2␀␀␀␀␀?ä2␀␀␀␀␀‡å2␀␀␀␀␀#è2␀␀␀␀␀…í2␀␀␀␀␀*ñ2␀␀␀␀␀∆ò2␀␀␀␀␀Vö2␀␀␀␀␀Ùú2␀␀␀␀␀;†2␀␀␀␀␀£2␀␀␀␀␀—£2␀␀␀␀␀Ê•2␀␀␀␀␀#ß2␀␀␀␀␀%©2␀␀␀␀␀àØ2␀␀␀␀␀≤2␀␀␀␀␀5∂2␀␀␀␀␀›∑2␀␀␀␀␀>º2␀␀␀␀␀˘Ω2␀␀␀␀␀bƒ2␀␀␀␀␀≈2␀␀␀␀␀~≈2␀␀␀␀␀y«2␀␀␀␀␀EÃ2␀␀␀␀␀‹Ã2␀␀␀␀␀rœ2␀␀␀␀␀{’2␀␀␀␀␀Ÿ2␀␀␀␀␀ŒŸ2␀␀␀␀␀Ñ⁄2␀␀␀␀␀‹2␀␀␀␀␀Ã‹2␀␀␀␀␀|›2␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ2␀␀␀␀␀≤ﬁ2␀␀␀␀␀<ﬂ2␀␀␀␀␀ë‡2␀␀␀␀␀Œ‚2␀␀␀␀␀s„2␀␀␀␀␀Ò„2␀␀␀␀␀•‰2␀␀␀␀␀ Á2␀␀␀␀␀$Ë2␀␀␀␀␀øÍ2␀␀␀␀␀ıÏ2␀␀␀␀␀vÔ2␀␀␀␀␀_2␀␀␀␀␀1Ò2␀␀␀␀␀„Ò2␀␀␀␀␀ÃÛ2␀␀␀␀␀WÙ2␀␀␀␀␀àı2␀␀␀␀␀wˆ2␀␀␀␀␀Î˘2␀␀␀␀␀ú˙2␀␀␀␀␀ÿ˝2␀␀␀␀␀å˛2␀␀␀␀␀oˇ2␀␀␀␀␀èˇ2␀␀␀␀␀n3␀␀␀␀␀3␀␀␀␀␀03␀␀␀␀␀j	3␀␀␀␀␀#
